我本会在你的表演里找找这些迹象。

504
00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:26.020
You know?
你知道吗？

505
00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:27.760
The secret one that I had.
我曾藏着那个秘密。

506
00:19:28.880 --> 00:19:29.440
All right.
好吧。

507
00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:30.940
Well, let's get into this episode.
好了，我们来聊聊这一集。

508
00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:35.840
We have the opening credits, which was interesting that they did not change for Nellie.
片头字幕里，内莉的部分竟然没做更改，这挺有意思的。

509
00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.760
Oh, we got a fan mail flurry about that, Angela.
哦，安吉拉，我们收到了好多关于这事的粉丝来信。

510
00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:39.380
Oh, yeah?
是吗？

511
00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:39.660
Really?
真的吗？

512
00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:40.300
We did.
确实如此。

513
00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:46.640
So many people wrote in to say, how come we didn't have Nellie as the final manager image
好多人写信来问，为什么内莉没有出现在片尾经理的画面里

514
00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:48.840
since we've done that with everyone else, including Creed?
既然我们对其他人（包括克里德）都这么做了？

515
00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:51.480
I thought about it, and here's my theory.
我想过了，这是我的推测。

516
00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:51.980
Okay.
好吧。

517
00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:56.740
If they set up her at the desk at the very top, it ruins the whole storyline and the
如果一开始就让她坐在桌前，那就剧透了整条故事线

518
00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:59.860
surprise that she's taking over Andy's job slowly but surely.
也破坏了她一步步接替安迪工作的悬念。

519
00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.460
Well, do you think she'll be there next week?
好吧，你觉得她下周会在那儿吗？

520
00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:04.380
That's what I'm curious about.
这也是我好奇的。

521
00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:04.900
Me too.
我也是。

522
00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:06.420
I didn't watch ahead.
我没有提前看。

523
00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:07.360
I didn't either.
我也没有。

524
00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:09.460
Well, find out next week.
好吧，下周见分晓。

525
00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:09.720
Yeah.
是啊。

526
00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:13.100
The episode starts with Jim and Pam arriving to work.
这一集以吉姆和帕姆到达公司开始。

527
00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:15.040
They got an extra breakfast sandwich.
他们多买了一个早餐三明治。

528
00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:16.300
Does anyone want it?
有人要吗？

529
00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:17.800
Guess who wants it?
猜猜谁想要？

530
00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:22.700
Nellie appears out of nowhere, and she's back, and she's eating their sandwich.
内莉不知从哪儿冒出来了，她回来了，而且在吃他们的三明治。

531
00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:24.280
And she does not like it.
并且她并不喜欢。

532
00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:25.600
She says it's disgusting.
她说这太恶心了。

533
00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:28.840
She says, you call this a King James breakfast pie?
她说，你们管这叫詹姆斯国王早餐派？

534
00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:30.760
I looked it up.
我查过了。

535
00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:31.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

536
00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:38.020
It's really weird because it's believed to have originated in England, and it's basically
真的很奇怪，因为它被认为起源于英国，基本上

537
00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:44.560
a pie, and it has layers of bacon, sausage, eggs, cheese, sometimes hash browns or mushrooms
就是一个派，里面有培根、香肠、鸡蛋、奶酪，有时还有薯饼或蘑菇

538
00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:45.880
all baked together.
全都烤在一起。

539
00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:46.700
Okay.
好吧。

540
00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:49.160
I don't understand how you take it on the go.
我不明白这怎么能当成随身带的便餐。

541
00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:53.340
I saw some pictures where it looked like a pizza pocket, where it was like pie on top
我看到一些图片看起来像披萨口袋，就是上下都是派皮

542
00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:56.800
and bottom, and then some that just look like a pie.
还有一些看起来就只是个普通的派。

543
00:20:56.800 --> 00:21:02.180
But I cannot get any origin story on the King James breakfast pie.
但我找不到任何关于詹姆斯国王早餐派的起源故事。

544
00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:04.160
Why is it called the King James breakfast pie?
为什么它叫詹姆斯国王早餐派？

545
00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.460
Who really invented it?
到底是谁发明的？

546
00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:11.280
Some people say it was like an American invention based on British breakfaSt.
有人说这是根据英国早餐改编的美国发明。

547
00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:11.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

548
00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:13.520
It was very frustrating.
这太让人抓狂了。

549
00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:15.140
It sounds good.
听起来不错。

550
00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:17.040
It really looked good.
看起来真的很不错。

551
00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:19.700
I didn't bake one, but you know.
我没有烤，不过你知道的。

552
00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:20.920
I'm so surprised.
我太惊讶了。

553
00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:23.820
Well, I'm so surprised you don't have it for all of us to try today.
好吧，我很惊讶你今天居然没带给我们大家尝尝。

554
00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:26.480
Well, you know, what's happening to you?
好吧，你知道的，你怎么了？

555
00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:27.120
I don't know.
我不知道。

556
00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:30.660
Nellie is also going to dig on the Houdini Museum.
内莉还要去探究胡迪尼博物馆。

557
00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:31.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

558
00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:34.220
And then she announces she's come to work in Scranton.
然后她宣布她来斯克兰顿工作了。

559
00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:38.880
Toby walks right up to her and introduces himself as Tony.
托比径直走到她面前，介绍自己叫托尼。

560
00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:40.600
We got so much mail about that.
我们收到了好多关于这事的邮件。

561
00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:41.880
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

562
00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:44.740
He so casually then tried to cover this up.
他当时居然那么随性地想掩盖过去。

563
00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:47.780
I thought, has he introduced himself as Tony before, and why would he?
我在想，他以前是不是也自我介绍叫过托尼，他为什么要这么做？

564
00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:49.460
Is this a Scranton Strangler clue?
这是斯克兰顿扼喉手的线索吗？

565
00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:53.040
Well, we had a fan theory from Natasha M.
嗯，我们收到了来自威尔士的娜塔莎·M的粉丝理论

566
00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:55.320
in Wales who said,
她说，

567
00:21:55.720 --> 00:21:58.580
I think maybe his name was Tony all along.
我觉得也许他一直以来都叫托尼。

568
00:21:59.100 --> 00:22:03.240
But someone called him Toby one day, and he just didn't correct them,
但有一天有人叫他托比，他当时就没纠正对方，

569
00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:06.380
and now it's spiraled, and he will be forever known as Toby
然后事情就失控了，他以后就会永远被称为托比

570
00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:08.200
instead of his real name of Tony.
而不是他真正的名字托尼。

571
00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:09.820
Natasha, that's hilarious.
娜塔莎，这太搞笑了。

572
00:22:09.820 --> 00:22:11.300
You totally flipped it.
你完全把情况反过来了。

573
00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:12.940
That is so funny.
这太好笑了。

574
00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:18.540
You know, I thought maybe Tony is his alternate identity.
你知道的，我觉得也许托尼是他的化身。

575
00:22:19.640 --> 00:22:21.020
Tony's a different guy.
托尼是另一个人。

576
00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:22.260
We all know Toby.
我们都认识托比。

577
00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:23.220
Like Jekyll and Hyde.
就像杰基尔和海德一样。

578
00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:23.440
Yeah.
是啊。

579
00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:24.220
Tony and Toby.
托尼和托比。

580
00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:24.800
Yeah.
是啊。

581
00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:25.620
Yeah.
是啊。

582
00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:28.240
We had a fan catch from Amanda A.
我们收到了来自北卡罗来纳州的阿曼达·A的粉丝发现

583
00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:30.240
in North Carolina who said,
她说，

584
00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:35.140
Toby seems to not know who Nellie is and introduces himself,
托比好像不认识内莉是谁还自我介绍，

585
00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:38.860
but didn't Toby already meet Nellie at the end of season seven in search committee
但托比不是已经在第七季结尾的寻人委员会里见过内莉了吗

586
00:22:38.860 --> 00:22:40.700
when she interviewed for the manager position?
当时她面试经理职位？

587
00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:41.860
Such a good catch.
真是个敏锐的发现。

588
00:22:41.860 --> 00:22:43.560
He sat across the table from her.
他就坐在她桌子对面。

589
00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:43.960
Yeah.
是啊。

590
00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:44.540
Yeah.
是啊。

591
00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:48.420
And also, doesn't he know she's the president of special projects?
而且，他难道不知道她是特别项目负责人吗？

592
00:22:48.620 --> 00:22:55.300
Like, as the HR manager, he sent a bunch of his employees to another state to work on a project.
作为人事经理，他把一堆员工派到另一个州去参与一个项目。

593
00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:57.100
Wouldn't he know who they're working under?
他难道不会知道他们的顶头上司是谁吗？

594
00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:57.620
Come on.
拜托。

595
00:22:57.700 --> 00:22:59.220
There'd be forms to fill out.
那得填一堆表格。

596
00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:00.320
There's definitely forMs.
绝对有一堆表格。

597
00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:01.540
There's so many forMs.
有太多的表格了。

598
00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:02.580
Yeah.
是啊。

599
00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:04.300
What's happening to Toby?
托比怎么了？

600
00:23:04.420 --> 00:23:04.900
I don't know.
我不知道。

601
00:23:05.500 --> 00:23:10.960
Well, Tony tells Nellie, welcome, find a desk, have a seat, and then we'll wait for Robert to arrive.
托尼对内莉说，欢迎，找张桌子坐下，然后我们等罗伯特来。

602
00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:14.820
Nellie notices there's an empty seat in Andy's office.
内莉发现安迪办公室里有个空位。

603
00:23:15.100 --> 00:23:16.680
She'll take that seat and that job.
她就要那个座位和那份工作。

604
00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:17.520
Yeah.
没错。

605
00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:19.680
She says her business philosophy is simple.
她说她的商业哲学很简单。

606
00:23:19.820 --> 00:23:22.120
If the seat is open, the job is open.
位置空着，工作就是空着的。

607
00:23:22.580 --> 00:23:25.500
That's how she came to briefly race a Formula One car.
她就是这样短暂地去跑了一场一级方程式赛车。

608
00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:26.200
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

609
00:23:26.820 --> 00:23:28.500
Slowest laps ever recorded.
创下了有史以来最慢的单圈纪录。

610
00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:29.160
Ever recorded.
有史以来。

611
00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:31.660
I love that it's like a record.
我喜欢这听起来就像个纪录。

612
00:23:31.900 --> 00:23:34.200
You are a record holder, in a sense.
从某种意义上说，你是纪录保持者。

613
00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:34.660
Exactly.
正是如此。

614
00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:39.180
Down in Tallahassee, Erin is walking out to get the newspaper.
在塔拉哈西，艾琳正走出去拿报纸。

615
00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:41.160
Alonzo drives by.
阿隆佐开车路过。

616
00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:43.120
She tries to make small talk with him.
她试图和他闲聊几句。

617
00:23:43.200 --> 00:23:44.120
He just keeps driving.
他直接开过去没停。

618
00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:45.060
Yes.
是的。

619
00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:48.100
Well, Alonzo was played by Alexander Sabaha.
阿隆佐由亚历山大·萨巴哈饰演。

620
00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:49.260
He did a great job.
他演得真棒。

621
00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:50.440
He did fantastic.
他演得太好了。

622
00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:52.740
I cracked up when he just kept going.
他直接开走的时候我笑喷了。

623
00:23:53.420 --> 00:23:56.980
And now, lady, I really have a special award to give out.
现在，女士，我真的要颁发一个特别奖。

624
00:23:57.280 --> 00:23:57.740
Okay.
好啊。

625
00:23:58.060 --> 00:23:58.860
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

626
00:23:59.080 --> 00:24:06.280
Because the award for the worst green screen in the run of our show goes to Erin's Talking
因为我们剧集里最烂绿幕奖得主就是艾琳的单人访谈

627
00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:06.720
Head.
镜头。

628
00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:08.440
Congratulations.
恭喜。

629
00:24:08.900 --> 00:24:09.460
Congratulations.
恭喜。

630
00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:11.720
This was a fan mail flurry.
这引发了一波粉丝来信热潮。

631
00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:13.860
I talked to Steve Burgess about it.
我和史蒂夫·伯吉斯聊过这事。

632
00:24:14.020 --> 00:24:19.140
He said, yeah, it was a talking head that they had to add later on a green screen.
他说，对，那是后来必须用绿幕补拍的一个访谈镜头。

633
00:24:19.140 --> 00:24:24.280
He said there were two talking heads that were added after we shot this episode, and this
他说在我们拍完这集之后有两处单人访谈是后补的，而这

634
00:24:24.280 --> 00:24:25.000
was one of them.
就是其中之一。

635
00:24:25.040 --> 00:24:30.640
And I don't know why they couldn't just walk over to the outside of Tom Melby's house.
我搞不懂为什么他们不直接走到汤姆·梅尔比家外面去拍。

636
00:24:30.800 --> 00:24:31.740
It was right there.
就在那儿啊。

637
00:24:32.280 --> 00:24:38.900
But I guess instead, they filmed it as a plate, and then they shot her talking head on a green
但我想他们大概是先拍了背景底片，然后在一个绿幕前

638
00:24:38.900 --> 00:24:39.220
screen.
拍了她的单人访谈。

639
00:24:39.220 --> 00:24:41.000
It was real awful.
真的很糟糕。

640
00:24:41.280 --> 00:24:42.600
It was so obvious.
太明显了。

641
00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:43.620
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

642
00:24:43.940 --> 00:24:48.600
I told you that when I was researching this episode, it was just like a lot of critical
我跟你说过，当我研究这一集的时候，看到了一堆尖锐的

643
00:24:49.200 --> 00:24:49.760
articles.
文章。

644
00:24:50.340 --> 00:24:53.960
This talking head came up a lot for its terrible green screen effect.
这个访谈镜头因为其糟糕的绿幕效果被频繁提及。

645
00:24:54.480 --> 00:24:56.160
Well, I get it.
好吧，我懂了。

646
00:24:57.160 --> 00:25:01.360
In this talking head, we're going to learn that Erin is a maid for an old lady.
在这个访谈里，我们会得知艾琳给一位老太太当女佣。

647
00:25:01.760 --> 00:25:05.760
Runs her errands, gets to clean all five rooms of the house, not to brag.
帮她跑腿，还得打扫房子里全部五个房间，真不是吹牛。

648
00:25:06.460 --> 00:25:08.200
Back at Dunder Mifflin, Robert arrives.
回到邓德米夫林，罗伯特到了。

649
00:25:08.360 --> 00:25:14.440
He greets Nellie, asks her how she's adjusting, and he says, I can't wait to find something fun
他向内莉打招呼，问她适应得怎么样，他说，我很期待能找点有趣的事

650
00:25:14.440 --> 00:25:15.360
for you to do here.
情给你在这里做。

651
00:25:15.940 --> 00:25:17.280
Yeah, and Nellie says, you know what?
对啊，然后内莉说，你知道吗？

652
00:25:17.280 --> 00:25:18.480
I've already taken care of that.
我已经把那件事处理好了。

653
00:25:18.640 --> 00:25:19.620
I found something.
我找到了点东西。

654
00:25:19.780 --> 00:25:20.420
I'm the manager.
我是经理。

655
00:25:21.160 --> 00:25:24.060
He says, we already have a manager, and I love this line.
他说，我们已经有一个经理了，我太喜欢这句台词了。

656
00:25:24.060 --> 00:25:25.340
She says, oh, really?
她说，哦，真的吗？

657
00:25:25.620 --> 00:25:30.220
Because it's 10 a.m., I've been in this office for an hour, and no one has come and sat in
因为现在是早上十点，我来这个办公室已经一个小时了，还没人来坐在

658
00:25:30.220 --> 00:25:30.740
my lap.
我腿上。

659
00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:34.300
I don't think you have a manager.
我觉得你们根本没有经理。

660
00:25:34.780 --> 00:25:37.400
By all standards, you don't have a manager.
无论从什么标准来看，你们都没有经理。

661
00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:40.700
Well, now everyone is really wondering where Andy is.
好了，现在大家都在纳闷安迪去哪儿了。

662
00:25:40.880 --> 00:25:43.620
You know, he's usually here by now, and they start to discuss.
你知道的，他平时这个时候已经到了，他们开始讨论起来。

663
00:25:44.060 --> 00:25:47.960
There were a few versions of this scene, and there's one where Ryan and Oscar really
这场戏有几个不同的版本，其中有一个版本里瑞恩和奥斯卡真的

664
00:25:47.960 --> 00:25:49.680
get into it, and I want you to hear it.
吵得很厉害，我想让你们听听。

665
00:25:50.480 --> 00:25:51.720
Has anyone talked to Andy?
有人跟安迪联系过吗？

666
00:25:52.040 --> 00:25:53.640
He's not returning any calls.
他一个电话都不回。

667
00:25:54.100 --> 00:25:55.220
I checked his Facebook.
我查了他的脸书。

668
00:25:55.440 --> 00:25:57.020
Status said, pump for Wednesday.
状态写着，为周三打气。

669
00:25:58.080 --> 00:25:58.780
Today's Thursday.
今天是星期四。

670
00:25:59.460 --> 00:26:03.580
I hate to take you to this place, but re-Andy, has anyone checked the morgue?
我本不想说这种话，但关于安迪的事，有人查过太平间吗？

671
00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:05.740
Oh, checking the morgue isn't a real thing.
哦，查太平间可不是常规操作。

672
00:26:05.960 --> 00:26:06.560
That's a real thing.
那才是常规操作。

673
00:26:06.680 --> 00:26:07.320
You're a policeman.
你又不是警察。

674
00:26:07.540 --> 00:26:08.140
No, anyone.
不，任何人都可以。

675
00:26:08.260 --> 00:26:10.180
You're just like, hey, can I look around?
你难道就是去说，嗨，我能四处看看吗？

676
00:26:10.340 --> 00:26:10.700
Anyone?
任何人？

677
00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:12.320
Yeah, and they have names on everything.
对啊，而且他们每样东西上都有名字。

678
00:26:12.400 --> 00:26:13.020
I didn't know your word was CSI.
我以前可不知道你的口头禅是犯罪现场调查。

679
00:26:13.020 --> 00:26:13.800
Then you go to the graveyard.
然后你就去墓地。

680
00:26:13.940 --> 00:26:14.600
Then you go to the graveyard.
然后你就去墓地。

681
00:26:14.740 --> 00:26:15.480
Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.
行了，行了，行了，行了，行了。

682
00:26:15.480 --> 00:26:16.700
You look for a cemetery plot.
你去找墓地穴位。

683
00:26:16.800 --> 00:26:17.200
Guys, all right.
伙计们，行了。

684
00:26:17.440 --> 00:26:17.500
Shh.
嘘。

685
00:26:21.400 --> 00:26:28.000
I don't know, but just all of Ryan's phrasing, too, when he's like, re-Andy, has anyone?
我不知道，但瑞恩的措辞太搞笑了，比如他说“关于安迪，有人……”

686
00:26:28.180 --> 00:26:30.400
Like, just the way he talks, I'm like, oh my God, Ryan.
就凭他说话的那个调调，我真的觉得，天呐，瑞恩。

687
00:26:31.280 --> 00:26:33.000
And I love that Oscar just called him out.
而且我很喜欢奥斯卡当场拆穿他。

688
00:26:33.120 --> 00:26:33.940
Like, this is not a thing.
就好像，这根本不是那么回事。

689
00:26:34.800 --> 00:26:37.380
Well, Robert calls his phone.
接着罗伯特打了他手机。

690
00:26:37.900 --> 00:26:40.160
Andy answers and says he is sick.
安迪接了电话，说他病了。

691
00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:42.700
But Robert says, I don't care.
但罗伯特说，我不在乎。

692
00:26:42.840 --> 00:26:43.660
Come to work anyway.
不管怎样，来上班。

693
00:26:44.140 --> 00:26:48.980
Yeah, and then Andy says, I'm just really sick, and I've got that, and hangs up on him.
对，然后安迪说，我是真的很不舒服，我那个……然后就把电话挂了。

694
00:26:49.160 --> 00:26:53.260
Yes, Andy hangs up, and then we reveal he is standing on a beach.
没错，安迪把电话挂了，然后我们镜头一转，发现他正站在海滩上。

695
00:26:53.580 --> 00:26:55.140
He says he's in Florida.
他说他在佛罗里达。

696
00:26:55.660 --> 00:26:56.840
He's here to get Aaron.
他是来找艾琳的。

697
00:26:57.040 --> 00:26:58.620
He's, like, shaving on the beach.
他居然在海滩上刮胡子。

698
00:26:58.760 --> 00:27:00.360
He's, like, standing in the ocean.
他就像那样站在海水里。

699
00:27:00.360 --> 00:27:05.480
Yeah, I guess he couldn't have gone to a gas station to do this or something.
对啊，我猜他本来可以去加油站或者别的地方做这事的。

700
00:27:05.680 --> 00:27:06.000
I don't know.
我也不知道。

701
00:27:06.100 --> 00:27:07.760
He needed to do it in the ocean water.
他必须得在海水里做这件事。

702
00:27:07.980 --> 00:27:10.960
By the way, I looked up shaving using salt water.
顺便说一句，我查了关于用盐水刮胡子的资料。

703
00:27:11.180 --> 00:27:11.860
Not recommended.
不推荐。

704
00:27:11.860 --> 00:27:13.040
I wouldn't think so.
我也觉得不该这样。

705
00:27:13.040 --> 00:27:13.740
It burns.
会很痛。

706
00:27:13.880 --> 00:27:14.260
Of course.
当然。

707
00:27:14.480 --> 00:27:19.800
They also say don't shave your legs right before you go in the ocean water, because salt can get in the pores and sting.
他们还说千万别在下海前刮腿毛，因为盐分会钻进毛孔里，引起刺痛。

708
00:27:20.180 --> 00:27:21.740
I think I've made that mistake.
我想我犯过那个错误。

709
00:27:21.940 --> 00:27:22.480
Me, too.
我也是。

710
00:27:23.060 --> 00:27:26.980
Okay, back to Andy's talking head here in the middle of the ocean.
好了，画面回到正坐在大洋中央的安迪的单人访谈。

711
00:27:26.980 --> 00:27:30.800
I think I caught a little line fumble that made it into the show.
我觉得我发现了一个漏网的台词失误，居然被剪进正片里了。

712
00:27:31.060 --> 00:27:36.300
I am curious, because we got a fan mail flurry about something Andy said.
我很好奇，因为我们收到了大批关于安迪某句话的粉丝来信。

713
00:27:36.500 --> 00:27:39.000
Okay, well, I did a little mom detective work.
好吧，我稍微做了一点妈妈侦探工作。

714
00:27:39.420 --> 00:27:43.860
So when Andy has his talking head, he says, I'm in Florida to get Aaron.
所以当安迪做单人访谈时，他说，我在佛罗里达接埃伦。

715
00:27:44.080 --> 00:27:50.840
As soon as I heard she wasn't coming back to Scranton, I jumped straight in my car and drove straight down till I hit the ocean.
一听说她不回斯克兰顿了，我立马跳进车里，一路狂飙直到撞见大海。

716
00:27:51.180 --> 00:27:52.500
My heart is my map.
我的心就是我的地图。

717
00:27:52.500 --> 00:27:58.140
Turns out, Tallahassee is about 200 miles inland, so I overshot a good amount.
结果呢，塔拉哈西距离内陆大约有200英里，所以我过头了不少。

718
00:27:58.300 --> 00:28:01.040
But still, not bad for a heart map, right?
不过话说回来，凭心形地图能开成这样，已经很不错了吧？

719
00:28:01.560 --> 00:28:02.180
Yes.
是的。

720
00:28:02.540 --> 00:28:02.980
Okay.
好吧。

721
00:28:03.300 --> 00:28:13.800
Our fan mail flurry, which I'm hoping you detectived, but I don't know, is that the closest beach to Tallahassee is only about 40 miles inland.
我们收到的粉丝来信狂潮——希望你也有所侦查，但我不太确定——指出距离塔拉哈西最近的海滩其实只有大约40英里内陆距离。

722
00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:14.520
That's right.
没错。

723
00:28:14.520 --> 00:28:20.900
So if he's 200 miles away from Tallahassee, people would like to know, where the heck did Andy go?
所以如果他距离塔拉哈西200英里，大家就很想知道，安迪到底跑哪儿去了？

724
00:28:21.120 --> 00:28:23.200
Okay, I'm on it, you guys.
好啦，这事包在我身上，各位。

725
00:28:23.560 --> 00:28:32.300
So, yes, we have discussed a little bit about Tallahassee in previous episodes, but I think they might have intended something a little different than the way it was interpreted.
所以，是的，我们在之前的剧集里稍微讨论过塔拉哈西，但我认为他们原本的意图可能跟实际观众理解的有点不一样。

726
00:28:32.520 --> 00:28:32.680
Oh!
哦！

727
00:28:32.680 --> 00:28:36.560
So, yes, the Gulf of Mexico is about 22 miles from Tallahassee.
所以，是的，墨西哥湾距离塔拉哈西大约有22英里。

728
00:28:36.680 --> 00:28:37.720
You can see water there.
你在那儿能看到水。

729
00:28:38.660 --> 00:28:44.760
The truest white sandy beach on the internet, apparently, people say is St. George Island, which is about 90 miles.
网民们公认最纯正的白沙滩，据说圣乔治岛大约有90英里远。

730
00:28:44.920 --> 00:28:46.620
But still, this is not 200 miles.
但即便如此，这也不是200英里。

731
00:28:46.820 --> 00:28:47.000
Right.
对的。

732
00:28:47.180 --> 00:28:47.900
I was curious.
我挺好奇的。

733
00:28:48.040 --> 00:28:49.940
Why would the writers write this?
编剧为什么要这么写？

734
00:28:50.100 --> 00:28:55.420
I went to the shooting draft to see if this talking head was scripted the way it aired, and this is what I found.
我翻看了拍摄剧本，想看看这段单人访谈是不是就按播出的那样写的，结果我发现了这个。

735
00:28:56.100 --> 00:28:58.420
Everything was the same except for this line.
除了这一句台词外，其他都一样。

736
00:28:59.020 --> 00:29:02.320
I overshot Tallahassee by about 200 miles.
我过头了塔拉哈西大约200英里。

737
00:29:03.040 --> 00:29:04.860
There's no mention of the word inland.
里面根本没有提到“内陆”这个词。

738
00:29:05.440 --> 00:29:09.140
And I think Ed as Andy was not supposed to say the word inland.
而且我认为扮演安迪的埃德本来是不应该说“内陆”这个词的。

739
00:29:09.340 --> 00:29:10.640
It wasn't scripted.
剧本里根本没有。

740
00:29:10.760 --> 00:29:16.100
I think maybe he just said that line in the moment, and maybe that was their best take, and they left it in.
我想他可能只是当时即兴说出了那句台词，也许那是他们拍得最好的一条，于是就留下了。

741
00:29:16.220 --> 00:29:19.460
But it does change this talking head.
但这确实改变了这个单人访谈的意思。

742
00:29:19.660 --> 00:29:21.680
So I spent a lot of time on Google Maps.
所以我花了很多时间在谷歌地图上研究。

743
00:29:21.800 --> 00:29:27.360
If you drive from Scranton, Pennsylvania, down to Florida, a straight shot down the coast,
如果你从宾夕法尼亚州的斯克兰顿开车一路南下到佛罗里达，沿着海岸线直直开下去，

744
00:29:27.360 --> 00:29:31.940
because Andy said he was driving straight down until he saw the ocean.
因为安迪说过他是径直开下去直到看到大海。

745
00:29:32.080 --> 00:29:32.240
Yep.
没错。

746
00:29:32.900 --> 00:29:38.080
Well, there is one beach town that is a straight shot down from Scranton, Pennsylvania,
好吧，确实有一个海滨小镇是从宾夕法尼亚州斯克兰顿径直开下来能到达的，

747
00:29:38.080 --> 00:29:45.840
but that is also 202 miles from Tallahassee with St. Augustine Beach, Florida.
但那里同时也距离塔拉哈西202英里，也就是佛罗里达州的圣奥古斯丁海滩。

748
00:29:45.840 --> 00:29:50.320
And that is my theory for where Andy is when he does this talking head.
这就是我对安迪做这段单人访谈时身在何处的推测。

749
00:29:51.140 --> 00:29:52.280
But I'm not done.
但我还没说完呢。

750
00:29:52.440 --> 00:29:52.940
Oh.
哦。

751
00:29:53.420 --> 00:29:54.440
I was curious.
我很好奇。

752
00:29:54.440 --> 00:30:00.160
How long would it have taken Andy to drive from Scranton, Pennsylvania, to St. Augustine Beach, Florida,
安迪从宾夕法尼亚州斯克兰顿开车到佛罗里达州圣奥古斯丁海滩，

753
00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:02.880
and then over to Tallahassee?
然后去塔拉哈西，需要花多长时间？

754
00:30:02.880 --> 00:30:06.940
The first leg of the drive is 981 miles, roughly.
第一段车程大约是981英里。

755
00:30:07.180 --> 00:30:11.660
The second part of the drive is 203 miles, to correct his overshot.
第二段车程是203英里，用来纠正他开过头的路程。

756
00:30:12.020 --> 00:30:17.040
And it's around 1,200 miles altogether and about an 18-hour drive.
总共大约是1200英里，车程大约18个小时。

757
00:30:17.360 --> 00:30:19.900
That got me wondering, how did Andy do this?
这让我不禁想知道，安迪是怎么做到的？

758
00:30:20.020 --> 00:30:21.340
Did he have to stay at a motel?
他得住在汽车旅馆吗？

759
00:30:21.480 --> 00:30:22.620
Did he drive straight through?
他是直接一口气开过去的吗？

760
00:30:22.960 --> 00:30:27.960
Well, there's a moment in Deleted Scenes that fills us in a little bit about how he did this drive.
嗯，《被删减片段》里有一个片段稍微向我们透露了他是怎么完成这段车程的。

761
00:30:28.860 --> 00:30:29.960
You must be tired.
你一定累了。

762
00:30:29.960 --> 00:30:30.820
Uh, no.
呃，没有。

763
00:30:31.040 --> 00:30:31.680
Actually, I'm not tired.
其实我不累。

764
00:30:31.880 --> 00:30:35.320
I had a 12-pack of this energy drink called Up Yours.
我喝了一打这种叫“去你的”的能量饮料。

765
00:30:35.600 --> 00:30:38.060
It has a picture of a hyena giving you the finger on the can.
罐子上画着一只对你竖中指的土狼。

766
00:30:38.780 --> 00:30:39.800
I feel weird.
我觉得怪怪的。

767
00:30:40.160 --> 00:30:41.280
It's juSt...
只是……

768
00:30:42.600 --> 00:30:49.380
So I guess Andy got himself a case of Up Yours and powered through the night.
所以我猜安迪给自己买了一箱“去你的”，然后硬撑着熬过了夜。

769
00:30:49.860 --> 00:30:53.360
Well, I mean, he's going to tell Aaron later he didn't stop at all.
我的意思是，他后来会告诉亚伦他根本没停车。

770
00:30:53.380 --> 00:30:55.120
And she's like, not even to pee?
然后亚伦会说，连小便都不用吗？

771
00:30:55.380 --> 00:30:56.520
Not even to pee?
连小便都不用吗？

772
00:30:56.980 --> 00:30:58.760
Even though he drank all that Up Yours?
尽管他喝了那么多“去你的”？

773
00:30:59.040 --> 00:31:00.240
Yeah, I don't know.
对，我不知道。

774
00:31:00.240 --> 00:31:04.560
So, Angela, this was very, very good detective work.
所以，安吉拉，这是一次非常非常棒的侦探工作。

775
00:31:04.760 --> 00:31:05.360
Thank you.
谢谢你。

776
00:31:05.560 --> 00:31:12.140
Now, people from Florida, you might tell me there's a different beach town that would be the first one that Andy would see.
现在，来自佛罗里达的朋友们，你们可能会告诉我，安迪看到的第一个海滩小镇其实是另一个地方。

777
00:31:12.140 --> 00:31:14.520
But that's the one I saw that was also...
但那是当时我看到的，而且它也……

778
00:31:14.520 --> 00:31:15.380
Because it's two things.
因为这是两回事。

779
00:31:15.500 --> 00:31:18.180
It's got to be straight south from Scranton along the coaSt.
它必须沿着海岸线从斯克兰顿一路向南。

780
00:31:18.180 --> 00:31:22.380
But then it's also got to be around 200 miles from Tallahassee.
但同时它还得距离塔拉哈西大约200英里。

781
00:31:22.520 --> 00:31:24.300
I think this was excellent work.
我觉得这工作干得太棒了。

782
00:31:25.880 --> 00:31:28.280
I can tell you where we actually shot this.
我可以告诉你们我们实际拍摄这个场景的地方。

783
00:31:28.500 --> 00:31:28.900
Oh, yes.
哦，太好了。

784
00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:29.860
Where was Ed?
艾德在哪里拍的？

785
00:31:30.200 --> 00:31:32.360
Ed was at Will Rogers Beach.
艾德在威尔罗杰斯海滩。

786
00:31:33.060 --> 00:31:38.240
And Steve Burgess said, we just sent a small crew, a splinter unit, as they're called.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，我们只派了一个小剧组，也就是所谓的独立小分队。

787
00:31:38.500 --> 00:31:42.780
It was two vans, one camera, sound, and a few props.
那是两辆面包车、一台摄像机、录音设备和一些道具。

788
00:31:42.780 --> 00:31:44.660
And Ed was there about two hours.
艾德在那里待了大约两个小时。

789
00:31:45.580 --> 00:31:48.060
Well, that was a lot of Google Maps for you guys.
好吧，你们俩可真没少查谷歌地图。

790
00:31:48.240 --> 00:31:49.460
Maybe we should take a break.
也许我们该休息一下了。

791
00:31:49.780 --> 00:31:56.560
Because when we come back, Robert is basically going to share with everyone he's not going to do anything about Nellie's takeover.
因为等我们回来后，罗伯特基本上要跟所有人宣布，他对奈莉的接管无能为力。

792
00:31:56.720 --> 00:31:57.840
Because you know what, Jenna?
因为你知道吗，珍娜？

793
00:31:58.060 --> 00:32:00.020
Sometimes the flowers arrange themselves.
有时花朵会自己排列好。

794
00:32:01.120 --> 00:32:01.520
Exactly.
没错。

795
00:32:03.060 --> 00:32:03.920
We'll take a break.
我们休息一下。

796
00:32:04.100 --> 00:32:04.700
Be right back.
马上回来。

797
00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:15.800
We're back.
我们回来了。

798
00:32:16.180 --> 00:32:19.000
And yeah, Robert is not going to take any action.
没错，罗伯特不打算采取任何行动。

799
00:32:19.340 --> 00:32:21.220
Jim is like, what the heck is going on?
吉姆的反应就像是，这到底是怎么回事？

800
00:32:21.780 --> 00:32:23.420
The wheels are coming off the bus.
局势彻底失控了。

801
00:32:23.980 --> 00:32:31.220
I think that little, where is Andy at the end of Jim's Talking Head, I feel like that was an improv.
我觉得吉姆面对镜头讲话结束时那个小小的、安迪在哪里，我觉得那是即兴发挥。

802
00:32:32.140 --> 00:32:32.940
Do you think?
你觉得吗？

803
00:32:33.540 --> 00:32:34.740
I didn't look it up.
我没去查。

804
00:32:34.840 --> 00:32:35.740
I should have looked it up.
我本该查一下的。

805
00:32:35.880 --> 00:32:36.420
I don't know.
我不知道。

806
00:32:36.500 --> 00:32:37.720
I feel like I could just tell.
我感觉我能看出来。

807
00:32:38.040 --> 00:32:39.640
But I'll tell you where Andy is.
但我告诉你安迪在哪里。

808
00:32:39.740 --> 00:32:41.140
Andy is in a box.
安迪在一个箱子里。

809
00:32:41.960 --> 00:32:45.100
Because Irene opens her front door, and there's a box.
因为艾琳打开了前门，然后有个箱子。

810
00:32:45.760 --> 00:32:47.120
There's no postage on it.
上面没有邮资。

811
00:32:47.800 --> 00:32:49.140
Yeah, it's a package.
对，是个包裹。

812
00:32:49.420 --> 00:32:50.340
It's for Aaron.
是给亚伦的。

813
00:32:50.600 --> 00:32:50.960
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

814
00:32:51.480 --> 00:32:54.000
And Andy is going to pop out with flowers.
然后安迪会带着花跳出来。

815
00:32:54.020 --> 00:32:56.940
And he's singing, Signs Sealed and Delivered.
他还在唱着《已签字、送达，属于你》。

816
00:32:57.180 --> 00:33:01.540
I love that no one in the house, like, saw him doing any shenanigans in the front yard.
我喜欢的是，屋里居然没人看到他在前院搞什么恶作剧。

817
00:33:01.720 --> 00:33:04.920
You know this was not a simple, like, oh, just set a box down.
你知道这绝不是那种简单地、哦，随便放下个箱子。

818
00:33:05.080 --> 00:33:08.400
It was like, I'm going to put a box, then I'm going to climb in it, then I'm going to try to tape it.
这就像是，我要放个箱子，然后我要爬进去，接着我要试着把它封好。

819
00:33:08.400 --> 00:33:09.880
Like, what's happening in the front yard?
话说，前院里到底在发生什么？

820
00:33:10.180 --> 00:33:12.280
You know, I didn't think about the moment before.
你知道的，我之前没想过前情铺垫。

821
00:33:12.580 --> 00:33:18.280
Moment before is what we're asked to imagine before we go on stage as an actor.
前情铺垫就是我们作为演员上台前被要求想象的东西。

822
00:33:18.460 --> 00:33:18.840
Yes.
是的。

823
00:33:18.980 --> 00:33:21.060
This is a big part of acting crap.
这是演戏这破事里很大的一部分。

824
00:33:21.180 --> 00:33:21.460
Crap.
破事。

825
00:33:21.640 --> 00:33:21.860
Yeah.
是的。

826
00:33:21.860 --> 00:33:24.420
What was my moment before I appeared?
我出场前的上一刻在干嘛？

827
00:33:24.680 --> 00:33:26.360
In my mind, Andy had stuff.
在我脑子里，安迪带了东西。

828
00:33:26.560 --> 00:33:28.100
There was, like, a roll of tape somewhere.
比如某个地方有一卷胶带。

829
00:33:28.380 --> 00:33:29.640
There was, I don't know.
还有，我不知道。

830
00:33:29.640 --> 00:33:32.060
Yeah, is it in the, how did he do it?
对啊，是不是在，他是怎么做到的？

831
00:33:32.220 --> 00:33:32.840
I don't know.
我不知道。

832
00:33:33.040 --> 00:33:34.860
I get hung up on the moment before.
我总是纠结于前情铺垫。

833
00:33:35.420 --> 00:33:38.240
Well, this moment before is a mystery.
好吧，这个前情铺垫是个谜。

834
00:33:38.980 --> 00:33:46.700
We had a fan question from Victoria Kaye in Wisconsin who wanted to know how much did we have to pay for the rights for Signs Sealed and Delivered?
我们收到了来自威斯康星州维多利亚·凯e的粉丝提问，她想知道我们为《已签字、送达，属于你》的版权付了多少钱？

835
00:33:46.700 --> 00:33:50.580
And the answer was $20,000.
答案是两万美元。

836
00:33:51.780 --> 00:33:53.980
It was a pricey song.
这是一首很贵的歌。

837
00:33:54.560 --> 00:34:00.960
However, I looked up a little history on Signs Sealed and Delivered, and I'm going to say it's worth every penny.
不过，我查了点关于《已签字、送达，属于你》的历史，我要说这每一分钱都花得值。

838
00:34:02.080 --> 00:34:07.820
This song was originally released in 1970, and it is a Motown classic.
这首歌最初发行于1970年，是一首摩城经典。

839
00:34:08.080 --> 00:34:14.920
It has a really interesting history because Stevie Wonder co-wrote this song with his wife, Sarita Wright.
它有着非常有趣的历史，因为史蒂维·旺德和他的妻子萨里塔·赖特共同创作了这首歌。

840
00:34:15.040 --> 00:34:19.600
They're no longer married, but after this song was released, they married just weeks later.
他们现在已经离婚了，但这首歌发行后仅几周他们就结婚了。

841
00:34:20.480 --> 00:34:31.840
He also co-wrote it with an occasional collaborator named Lee Garrett, but the song carries an additional co-writing credit for Stevie Wonder's mother, the late Lula Mae Hardaway,
他还和一位偶尔合作的伙伴李·加勒特共同创作了这首歌，但这首歌还有一个额外的署名，属于史蒂维·旺德的母亲、已故的露拉·梅·哈达韦，

842
00:34:32.080 --> 00:34:37.900
because Stevie Wonder said that she said the title phrase when she heard him working on the song's melody.
因为史蒂维·旺德说，当他听到母亲听到这首歌的旋律时，说出了歌名里的那句话。

843
00:34:37.900 --> 00:34:39.500
Oh, that's so cool.
哦，太酷了。

844
00:34:40.360 --> 00:34:50.600
And this was also a really significant song because it was the first single on which Stevie Wonder was listed as a producer, and it's also his first to win a Grammy nomination.
而且这也是一首非常重要的歌，因为它是史蒂维·旺德首次以制作人身份署名的单曲，也是他第一首获得格莱美提名的歌曲。

845
00:34:50.880 --> 00:34:52.560
It's a song with a lot of history.
这是一首有着深厚历史底蕴的歌。

846
00:34:52.760 --> 00:34:53.080
A lot of history.
底蕴深厚。

847
00:34:53.720 --> 00:34:56.760
And Andy is going to jump out of a box and sing it to Aaron.
而安迪要从箱子里跳出来，唱给亚伦听。

848
00:34:57.080 --> 00:34:57.380
Yep.
没错。

849
00:34:57.720 --> 00:34:58.320
With flowers.
还带着花。

850
00:34:58.620 --> 00:34:59.600
That's the other thing.
还有一件事。

851
00:34:59.700 --> 00:35:01.320
He had to crawl in the box with flowers.
他得钻进装满花的盒子里。

852
00:35:01.640 --> 00:35:03.240
He had to stop and get a box.
他不得不停下来去买个盒子。

853
00:35:03.240 --> 00:35:05.940
He had to get a Sharpie because he had to write on the outside of the box.
他不得不去拿支记号笔，因为他得在盒子外面写字。

854
00:35:05.940 --> 00:35:06.220
And tape.
还有胶带。

855
00:35:06.220 --> 00:35:10.640
Is it taped, or is it – how do you – did he get in from the bottom?
是用胶带封上的，还是——你怎么——他是从底部进去的吗？

856
00:35:11.480 --> 00:35:13.400
Maybe he got in from the bottom.
也许他是从底部钻进去的。

857
00:35:13.940 --> 00:35:18.860
Now, maybe he had some of these supplies at Dunder Mifflin, but it really looked like he just ran right out.
现在，也许他在邓德米夫林公司准备了一些这样的物资，但看起来他真的就像是直接冲出去的。

858
00:35:19.120 --> 00:35:22.080
Yeah, it didn't look like he grabbed supplies for a box.
对，看起来他不像特意准备了装盒子的物资。

859
00:35:22.360 --> 00:35:26.440
No, I think this was maybe an idea he had while he was drinking the up yours.
不，我觉得这可能是他喝着“少废话”饮料时想到的点子。

860
00:35:27.880 --> 00:35:30.260
Yeah, 12 hours into his drive.
对，在他开了12小时车之后。

861
00:35:31.400 --> 00:35:36.340
Well, once in the house, Andy is going to tell Aaron that he loves her and he wants to be with her.
好吧，一进屋，安迪就要告诉艾伦他爱她，他想和她在一起。

862
00:35:36.480 --> 00:35:37.680
He wants to be together.
他想厮守在一起。

863
00:35:37.860 --> 00:35:40.460
And he's there to take her home to Scranton.
他是来带她回斯克兰顿的。

864
00:35:41.040 --> 00:35:43.420
Irene says, where's the ring, Lancelot?
艾琳说，戒指呢，兰斯洛特？

865
00:35:43.560 --> 00:35:44.740
I loved that line.
我太喜欢这句台词了。

866
00:35:45.320 --> 00:35:46.800
And Aaron says, you know what?
然后艾伦说，你知道吗？

867
00:35:46.900 --> 00:35:49.160
Thanks, Andy, but I'm not going to go with you.
谢谢你，安迪，但我不会跟你走的。

868
00:35:50.340 --> 00:35:50.780
What?
什么？

869
00:35:52.510 --> 00:35:55.270
Can we play a few bullshit cards here?
我们能打几张扯淡牌吗？

870
00:35:55.650 --> 00:35:57.590
I mean, she's in love with him.
我的意思是，她深爱着他。

871
00:35:58.190 --> 00:35:58.370
Yeah.
对。

872
00:35:58.670 --> 00:36:00.210
He drives all the way there.
他一路开车过去。

873
00:36:00.450 --> 00:36:02.930
This is her moment to be like, no, not so much.
这是她表态的时候，结果来了句：不，没那么喜欢。

874
00:36:03.310 --> 00:36:08.930
This is where, if they'd had me, they would have lost me.
如果是我的话，这里就会让我粉转黑了。

875
00:36:09.250 --> 00:36:11.850
Because I don't need all this.
因为我不需要这一切。

876
00:36:12.010 --> 00:36:15.090
Like, there's this much cat and mouse in your relationship.
比如，你们的关系里有这么多的猫鼠游戏。

877
00:36:15.390 --> 00:36:16.490
You're not meant to be together.
你们根本不适合在一起。

878
00:36:16.490 --> 00:36:17.250
Don't do it.
别这么做。

879
00:36:17.410 --> 00:36:17.950
Like, truly.
真的。

880
00:36:18.330 --> 00:36:18.510
Yeah.
对。

881
00:36:18.910 --> 00:36:24.570
You can't spend your whole relationship with someone just waiting and waiting and waiting
你不能把和某人的整段关系都耗在无尽的等待上

882
00:36:24.570 --> 00:36:25.390
for them to chase you.
等着他们来追你。

883
00:36:25.470 --> 00:36:27.850
And then when they do, you punish them by rejecting them.
然后当他们真的追来时，你却用拒绝来惩罚他们。

884
00:36:28.050 --> 00:36:30.650
Like, that's a cycle we don't need.
这种死循环我们不需要。

885
00:36:30.810 --> 00:36:31.070
No.
对。

886
00:36:31.230 --> 00:36:32.450
That's not a happy life.
那不是幸福的生活。

887
00:36:32.590 --> 00:36:35.930
I have to say, I don't think there's that cycle with Jessica.
我得说，我觉得和杰西卡在一起没有这种循环。

888
00:36:36.430 --> 00:36:38.110
Of course there's not that cycle with Jessica.
和杰西卡在一起当然没有这种循环。

889
00:36:38.330 --> 00:36:38.790
I know.
我知道。

890
00:36:39.030 --> 00:36:41.190
We clearly need t-shirts that say Team Jessica.
我们显然需要印着“杰西卡战队”的T恤。

891
00:36:41.190 --> 00:36:41.470
Team Jessica.
杰西卡战队。

892
00:36:41.730 --> 00:36:42.570
Because we are.
因为我们就是。

893
00:36:42.790 --> 00:36:46.350
We've had a few people point out to us that we are clearly Team Jessica.
已经有不少人向我们指出，我们显然是杰西卡战队的。

894
00:36:46.490 --> 00:36:47.010
Sorry.
抱歉。

895
00:36:47.390 --> 00:36:47.910
We are.
我们就是。

896
00:36:48.710 --> 00:36:53.090
Back in Scranton, Nellie is going to lead a conference room meeting called What is Going
回到斯克兰顿，内莉要在会议室主持一场名为“到底怎么了？”的会议。

897
00:36:53.090 --> 00:36:53.430
On?
到底怎么了？

898
00:36:53.810 --> 00:36:55.330
What is going on?
到底怎么了？

899
00:36:55.390 --> 00:36:58.830
I would love to sit in a meeting called What is Going On?
我很乐意去参加一个名叫“到底怎么了？”的会议。

900
00:36:59.210 --> 00:37:00.290
That's pretty funny.
挺搞笑的。

901
00:37:01.330 --> 00:37:04.350
Yeah, she asks everyone, does anyone know what's going on?
对，她问所有人，有人知道发生了什么吗？

902
00:37:04.510 --> 00:37:06.470
Kevin and a few people raised their hands.
凯文和另外几个人举起了手。

903
00:37:06.570 --> 00:37:07.390
What are they going to say?
他们会说些什么呢？

904
00:37:07.530 --> 00:37:09.210
I wish we could have called on them.
我真希望当时能点他们发言。

905
00:37:09.330 --> 00:37:10.810
My character raises her hand.
我的角色举起了手。

906
00:37:10.950 --> 00:37:12.410
I think I just did it just for fun.
我想我当时只是好玩才这么做的。

907
00:37:12.530 --> 00:37:13.850
What is Angela Martin going to say?
安吉拉·马丁会说什么呢？

908
00:37:14.230 --> 00:37:15.930
Well, Nellie calls on Kevin.
好吧，奈莉点名了凯文。

909
00:37:15.930 --> 00:37:17.190
She's going to guess his name.
她打算猜他的名字。

910
00:37:17.370 --> 00:37:18.670
She's going to call him Chumbo.
她打算叫他“笨大个”。

911
00:37:19.050 --> 00:37:21.430
This made me wonder, is Chumbo a name?
这让我不禁琢磨，Chumbo是一个名字吗？

912
00:37:21.610 --> 00:37:26.590
It's clearly meant as a joke in our script, but is anyone named Chumbo?
在我们的剧本里这显然是个笑话，但真有人叫Chumbo吗？

913
00:37:26.990 --> 00:37:29.130
I did not wonder about this, Jenna.
我可没琢磨这个，珍娜。

914
00:37:29.390 --> 00:37:32.350
I did wonder about maps, but I know.
我琢磨过地图，不过我知道。

915
00:37:32.570 --> 00:37:34.470
What do you got in the name department?
你在名字方面有什么发现吗？

916
00:37:34.470 --> 00:37:42.150
Well, according to the Urban Dictionary, it is a slang term that is used in the gay community
嗯，根据《城市词典》，这是一个在同性恋社群中使用的俚语

917
00:37:42.150 --> 00:37:45.350
to describe a ridiculously straight man.
用来形容一个荒谬的直男。

918
00:37:45.790 --> 00:37:46.250
Oh.
哦。

919
00:37:46.830 --> 00:37:50.550
I called a gay friend of mine to check this out.
我给一个同性恋朋友打了电话来核实这件事。

920
00:37:50.750 --> 00:37:51.170
You.
你呀。

921
00:37:52.050 --> 00:37:52.930
Stop it.
别闹了。

922
00:37:53.970 --> 00:37:54.410
Stop.
住手。

923
00:37:54.870 --> 00:37:57.330
This is the most mom moment.
这太有当妈的既视感了。

924
00:37:57.870 --> 00:37:58.350
I know.
我知道。

925
00:37:58.530 --> 00:37:59.130
Honey, kids, listen.
亲爱的，孩子们，听着。

926
00:37:59.290 --> 00:38:01.830
I called my gay friend, and here's what he said.
我打了电话给我同性恋朋友，他是这么说的。

927
00:38:02.050 --> 00:38:07.130
Well, we've been friends since college, so I felt like I could call him with this research
好吧，我们从大学起就是朋友了，所以我觉得我可以为这个研究

928
00:38:07.130 --> 00:38:07.690
question.
问题打电话咨询他。

929
00:38:08.050 --> 00:38:14.190
And he said, Jenna, I've never heard it, but I'm in my 50s, and I don't always have my finger
他说，珍娜，我从没听说过，但我已经五十多岁了，并不总能掌握

930
00:38:14.190 --> 00:38:17.850
on the pulse of the hip, younger gay community.
年轻时髦的同性恋社群的最新脉搏。

931
00:38:18.070 --> 00:38:20.990
It could be that Chumbo is being thrown out all the time.
可能Chumbo这个词一直都在被广泛使用。

932
00:38:20.990 --> 00:38:22.430
He said, I've not used it.
他说，我没用过。

933
00:38:23.070 --> 00:38:29.310
But yeah, according to Urban Dictionary, Chumbos tend to be womanizing, beer drinking, steak
不过好吧，根据《城市词典》，Chumbos往往是好色、喝啤酒、吃牛排

934
00:38:29.310 --> 00:38:32.350
eating, American football watching heterosexists.
看美式足球的异性恋至上主义者。

935
00:38:33.650 --> 00:38:38.750
Heterosexist would mean that you have to be all those things, and then also, I guess, homophobic.
异性恋至上主义意味着你必须具备所有这些特征，然后，我猜，还有恐同倾向。

936
00:38:39.690 --> 00:38:40.170
Yeah.
对。

937
00:38:40.490 --> 00:38:41.350
Oh, I see.
哦，原来如此。

938
00:38:41.530 --> 00:38:42.790
Yeah, that's a Chumbo.
对，那就是个Chumbo。

939
00:38:43.590 --> 00:38:44.590
I don't know.
我不知道。

940
00:38:44.790 --> 00:38:47.770
According to the Cambridge Dictionary, Chumbo means lead.
根据《剑桥词典》，Chumbo的意思是铅。

941
00:38:48.950 --> 00:38:50.970
Lead, like L-E-A-D?
铅，就像L-E-A-D那样？

942
00:38:51.270 --> 00:38:53.650
Lead as in the material.
铅，指这种材料。

943
00:38:53.850 --> 00:38:54.830
Like lead poisoning.
比如铅中毒。

944
00:38:55.270 --> 00:38:55.570
Right.
没错。

945
00:38:55.910 --> 00:38:56.190
Okay.
好吧。

946
00:38:56.550 --> 00:38:57.610
Yes, lead paint.
是的，含铅油漆。

947
00:38:58.490 --> 00:39:00.250
Yeah, Chumbo.
对，Chumbo。

948
00:39:00.610 --> 00:39:02.730
In Portuguese, it means prickly pear.
在葡萄牙语里，它的意思是仙人掌果。

949
00:39:03.090 --> 00:39:06.010
Could I get a Chumbo, please, with my breakfast?
能给我来个Chumbo吗，伴着我的早餐？

950
00:39:06.930 --> 00:39:09.290
I would like a Chumbo salad.
我想要一份Chumbo沙拉。

951
00:39:09.770 --> 00:39:10.310
Okay.
好的。

952
00:39:10.310 --> 00:39:11.530
One more thing.
还有一件事。

953
00:39:11.690 --> 00:39:17.090
If you put the name Chumbo into meaningslike.com, this is a website that tells you the meaning
如果你把“Chumbo”这个名字输入 meaningslike.com，这是一个告诉你名字含义的网站。

954
00:39:17.090 --> 00:39:17.690
of names.
名字的含义。

955
00:39:17.890 --> 00:39:20.310
It says a definition.
上面写着一个定义。

956
00:39:20.750 --> 00:39:28.310
It says, people named Chumbo represent ambitious independence, strength, reliability, and professionalism.
它写着，名叫 Chumbo 的人代表着雄心勃勃的独立性、力量、可靠性和专业精神。

957
00:39:28.310 --> 00:39:30.550
This sounds like a bogus website.
这听起来像个虚假的网站。

958
00:39:30.790 --> 00:39:31.550
It was.
确实是。

959
00:39:31.870 --> 00:39:35.770
I put my name in, and I put in Regina.
我输入了我的名字，我还输入了雷吉娜。

960
00:39:36.190 --> 00:39:36.550
Yeah.
对。

961
00:39:36.690 --> 00:39:37.770
Regina means queen.
雷吉娜的意思是女王。

962
00:39:38.110 --> 00:39:38.990
It didn't say that.
它可没这么说。

963
00:39:39.170 --> 00:39:45.630
I feel like I could put in, like, stinky shoe, and it would say, this is a name that would lead nations.
我觉得就算我输入“臭鞋子”之类的词，它也会说，这是一个能领导国家的伟大名字。

964
00:39:45.630 --> 00:39:48.450
Yes, I did get that feeling.
是的，我确实有这种感觉。

965
00:39:48.690 --> 00:39:56.370
I also couldn't find anyone with the first name Chumbo, but I did find Chumbo as a last name a few times.
我也找不到任何名字叫 Chumbo 的人，但确实在几次记录中看到 Chumbo 作为姓氏出现。

966
00:39:56.570 --> 00:39:57.030
Okay.
好吧。

967
00:39:57.030 --> 00:39:59.130
Back in, like, ye olden times.
回溯到很久很久以前。

968
00:39:59.350 --> 00:39:59.710
Ye olden times.
很久很久以前。

969
00:39:59.710 --> 00:40:00.730
There were some Chumbos.
确实有一些叫 Chumbo 的人。

970
00:40:01.290 --> 00:40:02.690
So, Charles Chumbo.
所以，查尔斯·琼博。

971
00:40:03.210 --> 00:40:03.730
Yeah.
对。

972
00:40:04.030 --> 00:40:04.270
Okay.
好。

973
00:40:04.550 --> 00:40:06.750
Charles Chumbo ate a prickly pear.
查尔斯·琼博吃了一个仙人掌果。

974
00:40:06.970 --> 00:40:09.070
Ate a prickly pear in Portugal.
在葡萄牙吃了一个仙人掌果。

975
00:40:09.670 --> 00:40:10.230
Yes.
没错。

976
00:40:10.410 --> 00:40:11.730
While wearing a lead ring.
同时戴着一枚铅戒指。

977
00:40:12.590 --> 00:40:13.650
I guess.
我猜吧。

978
00:40:14.290 --> 00:40:15.790
And watching football.
并且在看橄榄球。

979
00:40:16.510 --> 00:40:16.990
Exactly.
完全正确。

980
00:40:18.110 --> 00:40:19.470
What has happened to us?
我们怎么变成这样了？

981
00:40:19.610 --> 00:40:20.330
I don't know.
我不知道。

982
00:40:20.550 --> 00:40:21.270
We're like Andy.
我们就像安迪一样。

983
00:40:21.450 --> 00:40:22.070
We're loopy.
我们脑子发热了。

984
00:40:22.210 --> 00:40:22.890
We're loopy.
我们脑子糊涂了。

985
00:40:23.030 --> 00:40:23.210
Okay.
好吧。

986
00:40:23.670 --> 00:40:29.310
Well, Nellie is going to explain to Chumbo and everyone else that she is the new manager.
那么，内莉要向琼博和其他所有人宣布她就是新经理。

987
00:40:29.650 --> 00:40:39.090
Pam asked Robert if this is true, and Robert is doing that thing that he does where clearly life is just, like, entertainment for him.
帕姆问罗伯特这是不是真的，而罗伯特又在搞他那套把戏，对明显的生活而言，这一切对他来说不过是一场娱乐。

988
00:40:39.230 --> 00:40:41.050
And now he's finally entertained.
现在他终于觉得有意思了。

989
00:40:41.350 --> 00:40:41.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

990
00:40:41.590 --> 00:40:43.690
He's been bored and asleep, but what?
他之前一直觉得无聊又困倦，但现在呢？

991
00:40:43.790 --> 00:40:43.950
What?
什么？

992
00:40:44.050 --> 00:40:44.630
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

993
00:40:44.790 --> 00:40:45.450
Something's happening.
有情况发生了。

994
00:40:45.790 --> 00:40:51.070
Robert says, in a world of routines and rhythms, Kevin eats someone's lunch.
罗伯特说，在这个充满日常和节奏的世界里，凯文吃掉了别人的午餐。

995
00:40:51.530 --> 00:40:52.970
Phyllis has a new necklace.
菲利丝有一条新项链。

996
00:40:53.830 --> 00:40:56.030
But who is this woman?
但这个女人是谁？

997
00:40:56.610 --> 00:40:56.990
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

998
00:40:57.250 --> 00:40:57.970
He's in.
他入戏了。

999
00:40:58.110 --> 00:40:59.450
He's like, I've just bought my ticket.
他的样子就像是，我刚买好票。

1000
00:40:59.450 --> 00:41:00.770
I'm going to watch this show.
我要好好看这场戏。

1001
00:41:00.990 --> 00:41:04.930
So, this was the other talking head that was added later in reshoots.
所以，这是后来补拍时加的另一个单人访谈镜头。

1002
00:41:05.070 --> 00:41:05.430
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1003
00:41:05.450 --> 00:41:08.610
This Robert talking head outside by the Dunder Mifflin sign.
这个罗伯特在邓德米弗林招牌外面的单人访谈镜头。

1004
00:41:08.830 --> 00:41:10.070
Well, I think we needed it.
嗯，我觉得我们需要它。

1005
00:41:10.250 --> 00:41:15.250
I do, too, because even with this talking head, a lot of the articles that I read,
我也觉得，因为即使有了这个单人访谈，我读到的很多文章里，

1006
00:41:15.250 --> 00:41:21.310
thought it was a little bit of a stretch that Robert was so permissive of this takeover by Nellie.
都觉得罗伯特对内莉接管公司表现得这么纵容有点牵强。

1007
00:41:21.690 --> 00:41:21.830
Right.
对。

1008
00:41:21.830 --> 00:41:23.310
This kind of explains it.
这就解释得通了。

1009
00:41:23.450 --> 00:41:25.070
Like you said, it's for his entertainment.
就像你说的，这是为了供他娱乐。

1010
00:41:25.070 --> 00:41:26.990
The world is here to entertain him.
这个世界就是用来取悦他的。

1011
00:41:27.110 --> 00:41:27.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1012
00:41:27.310 --> 00:41:29.910
But people had a little bit of a hard time with that.
但人们对这一点还是有点难以接受。

1013
00:41:30.170 --> 00:41:34.310
Well, here Nellie is in her first ever conference room meeting that she set up,
好啦，这里是内莉召开的她的第一场会议，

1014
00:41:34.350 --> 00:41:36.570
and she's going to tell people she feels disrespected.
她要告诉大家她觉得自己受到了不尊重。

1015
00:41:37.510 --> 00:41:42.270
And all she's trying to do is get to know everyone, and I'm sorry, but they've left her no choice.
而她所做的只是一起去了解每个人，对不起，但他们别无选择。

1016
00:41:42.750 --> 00:41:44.970
She's going to have to conduct performance reviews.
她不得不进行绩效考核。

1017
00:41:45.250 --> 00:41:45.430
Oh!
噢！

1018
00:41:45.570 --> 00:41:46.830
Oh, I forgot to say something.
噢，我忘了说件事。

1019
00:41:47.050 --> 00:41:47.370
What?
什么事？

1020
00:41:47.370 --> 00:41:50.410
But did you notice anything about this whole conference room scene?
但你有没有注意到整个会议室场景有什么特别的？

1021
00:41:50.590 --> 00:41:53.090
Did you see where we were seated?
你看到我们坐在哪儿了吗？

1022
00:41:53.450 --> 00:41:54.590
Yes, we were next to each other.
看到了，我们挨着坐在一起。

1023
00:41:54.590 --> 00:41:55.430
Yes, yes, I noticed that.
对，对，我注意到了。

1024
00:41:55.490 --> 00:41:56.110
I noticed that.
我注意到了。

1025
00:41:56.270 --> 00:41:57.690
It's been so long.
好久不见了。

1026
00:41:57.850 --> 00:41:59.250
I can't believe they let us do it.
真不敢相信他们会让我们这么坐。

1027
00:41:59.410 --> 00:42:01.310
Yeah, I totally meant to bring that up.
对，我本完全打算提起这个的。

1028
00:42:01.570 --> 00:42:01.910
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1029
00:42:02.610 --> 00:42:03.610
Seated next to each other.
坐在一起。

1030
00:42:03.690 --> 00:42:04.070
I know.
我知道。

1031
00:42:04.370 --> 00:42:05.130
But you're right.
但你说得对。

1032
00:42:05.270 --> 00:42:09.810
She's going to start conducting performance reviews, and she says smiling goes a long way.
她要开始进行绩效考核了，她说微笑大有帮助。

1033
00:42:10.170 --> 00:42:11.270
So think about smiling.
所以想想微笑吧。

1034
00:42:17.370 --> 00:42:17.970
Tiny performance.
微小的表演。

1035
00:42:18.470 --> 00:42:18.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1036
00:42:18.750 --> 00:42:19.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1037
00:42:19.330 --> 00:42:24.050
We're now going to get a real disgusting lunch from Erin.
我们现在要吃艾琳送来的一顿极其恶心的午餐了。

1038
00:42:24.410 --> 00:42:25.510
It's hot dogs.
是热狗。

1039
00:42:25.730 --> 00:42:26.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1040
00:42:26.130 --> 00:42:28.090
She's been reusing the hot dog water.
她一直在重复使用煮热狗的水。

1041
00:42:28.310 --> 00:42:29.630
It really gives it a lot more flavor.
这确实增添了很多风味。

1042
00:42:29.870 --> 00:42:31.550
It's only going to get better, she says.
她说，只会越来越好。

1043
00:42:31.890 --> 00:42:33.490
There's so much more to this scene.
这个场景里还有很多内容。

1044
00:42:33.650 --> 00:42:34.850
It's in Deleted Scenes.
在已删减片段里。

1045
00:42:35.330 --> 00:42:38.910
They wrote Glenn as such an asshole.
他们把格伦写得像个彻头彻尾的混蛋。

1046
00:42:39.190 --> 00:42:40.790
I think they had to dial it back.
我想他们不得不收敛一点。

1047
00:42:41.090 --> 00:42:44.190
I loved watching Glenn in this scene.
我很喜欢看格伦在这场戏里的表现。

1048
00:42:44.190 --> 00:42:46.430
I loved all of his facial expressions.
我喜欢他所有的面部表情。

1049
00:42:47.410 --> 00:42:49.190
I was eating it up.
我简直乐在其中。

1050
00:42:49.330 --> 00:42:53.650
He has a line in Deleted Scenes where they're all talking, and he goes,
他在已删减片段里有一句台词，当时大家都在说话，他说，

1051
00:42:54.870 --> 00:42:56.810
does anyone have anything I can read?
有人有什么东西能让我读读吗？

1052
00:42:56.810 --> 00:42:59.350
Because I'm not into this conversation.
因为我对这个谈话没兴趣。

1053
00:42:59.810 --> 00:43:01.010
I'm not here for it.
我可不掺和这个。

1054
00:43:01.230 --> 00:43:04.950
I have a little trivia about Glenn, the character of Glenn.
关于格伦，也就是格伦这个角色，我有一点冷知识。

1055
00:43:05.130 --> 00:43:05.370
Okay.
好吧。

1056
00:43:05.670 --> 00:43:09.010
You know, sometimes when the writers would write early versions of the script,
你知道的，有时候编剧在写剧本的早期版本时，

1057
00:43:09.270 --> 00:43:14.450
they would put in the name of a friend or someone that they imagined in the role.
他们会把一个朋友的名字或者他们想象中适合这个角色的人写进去。

1058
00:43:14.690 --> 00:43:14.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1059
00:43:14.910 --> 00:43:17.810
So in the early outline for this script, it said,
所以在早期这个剧本的大纲里，上面写着：

1060
00:43:18.450 --> 00:43:22.190
cut to Irene's 45-year-old son, Phil Rosenthal.
镜头切到艾琳45岁的儿子菲尔·罗森塔尔。

1061
00:43:23.990 --> 00:43:25.090
That's very funny.
这太好笑了。

1062
00:43:26.230 --> 00:43:30.430
But Irene's grandson was actually played by the very funny Brad Morris.
但艾琳的孙子实际上是由非常搞笑的布拉德·莫里斯饰演的。

1063
00:43:30.770 --> 00:43:32.630
He was a member of Second City Chicago.
他是芝加哥第二城剧团的成员。

1064
00:43:32.650 --> 00:43:36.090
He's also had recurring roles on Cougar Town and The Good Place.
他还在《熟女镇》和《善地》中出演过常驻角色。

1065
00:43:36.390 --> 00:43:37.370
Well, he's really funny.
嗯，他真的很搞笑。

1066
00:43:37.530 --> 00:43:40.070
There's a lot more of his character in Deleted Scenes.
在删减片段里有更多关于他角色的戏份。

1067
00:43:40.070 --> 00:43:42.270
He's just a real jerk, but it's hilarious.
他简直是个不折不扣的混蛋，但太爆笑了。

1068
00:43:42.810 --> 00:43:46.770
I do love that in this scene, Irene calls Andy out.
我真的很喜欢这场戏里艾琳当面戳穿安迪。

1069
00:43:47.030 --> 00:43:52.550
She says, so, Andrew, how does your skinny brunette girlfriend Jessica feel about you visiting your ex-girlfriend?
她说，那么，安迪，你那个身材苗条的黑发女朋友杰西卡，对你去看望前女友作何感想？

1070
00:43:53.290 --> 00:43:55.790
Andy says, we're not really dating anymore.
安迪说，我们其实已经不算在交往了。

1071
00:43:56.010 --> 00:44:00.310
So basically, I mean, I just have to cross a few T's and dot a few I's.
所以基本上，我是说，我只是得把一些收尾工作做好。

1072
00:44:00.310 --> 00:44:04.430
And Erin's like, wait, so you came to get me and you still have a girlfriend?
然后艾琳就像是，等等，所以你是来找我复合，却依然有个女朋友？

1073
00:44:05.370 --> 00:44:05.850
Andy.
安迪。

1074
00:44:06.250 --> 00:44:06.730
Andy!
安迪！

1075
00:44:07.470 --> 00:44:07.950
Yeah.
对。

1076
00:44:08.830 --> 00:44:11.410
Andy would have had a talking head after this scene.
这场戏之后安迪本来应该有一个面对镜头的独白访谈。

1077
00:44:11.690 --> 00:44:12.810
It's in Deleted Scenes.
它在删减片段里。

1078
00:44:12.850 --> 00:44:13.710
I want you to hear it.
我想让你们听听。

1079
00:44:14.570 --> 00:44:19.150
Irene knows all about Jessica, which means that Aaron has been talking about me a lot.
艾琳对杰西卡的事了如指掌，这意味着亚伦一直在滔滔不绝地谈论我。

1080
00:44:19.150 --> 00:44:20.910
Does that sound like someone who's moved on?
这听起来像是一个已经放下过去的人吗？

1081
00:44:22.950 --> 00:44:26.890
Do you even want dessert or are you still doing South Beach?
你到底还想不想要甜点，还是说你还在实行南海滩减肥法？

1082
00:44:30.870 --> 00:44:33.550
So, Aaron's clearly been talking about him quite a bit.
所以，亚伦显然一直在喋喋不休地谈论他。

1083
00:44:33.610 --> 00:44:37.070
But also, I did think it was funny that we learned he's on South Beach diet.
不过同时，我觉得好笑的是，我们了解到他在实行南海滩减肥法。

1084
00:44:37.990 --> 00:44:39.370
What's the South Beach diet?
什么是南海滩减肥法？

1085
00:44:39.530 --> 00:44:40.030
I can't remember.
我记不清了。

1086
00:44:40.110 --> 00:44:41.370
I know it was like a big fad.
我知道这曾是一阵巨大的风潮。

1087
00:44:41.550 --> 00:44:44.410
It's so funny to me, these diets that like come around, right?
我觉得这些流行一阵子的减肥法太逗了，对吧？

1088
00:44:44.490 --> 00:44:45.350
What am I eating now?
我现在到底在吃什么？

1089
00:44:45.350 --> 00:44:49.350
I feel like I remember my mom had the book, but what am I not eating, I guess?
我好像记得我妈买过那本书，但我猜，到底是什么不能吃来着？

1090
00:44:49.430 --> 00:44:50.430
Here, I Googled it.
给，我用谷歌查了一下。

1091
00:44:50.530 --> 00:44:54.290
So, it was a popular diet created by a cardiologiSt.
所以，这是一个由心脏病专家创立的流行减肥法。

1092
00:44:54.290 --> 00:44:56.430
There was a book, The South Beach Diet.
当时有一本书叫《南海滩减肥法》。

1093
00:44:56.850 --> 00:45:02.810
And I guess basically, this diet is lower in carbs and higher in protein and healthy fats.
我猜基本上，这种减肥法碳水化合物含量较低，蛋白质和健康脂肪含量较高。

1094
00:45:03.590 --> 00:45:05.190
So, it's just every other diet.
所以，不就是跟别的减肥法一样嘛。

1095
00:45:06.010 --> 00:45:07.550
I mean, that's every diet, right?
我是说，所有的减肥法不都这样吗，对吧？

1096
00:45:08.130 --> 00:45:09.250
Isn't that paleo?
那不就是旧石器饮食法吗？

1097
00:45:09.410 --> 00:45:10.490
Isn't paleo the same thing?
旧石器饮食法难道不是一回事吗？

1098
00:45:10.490 --> 00:45:11.230
I don't even know.
我甚至都不知道了。

1099
00:45:11.230 --> 00:45:19.530
It says, if you are doing the South Beach diet, you focus on eating lean proteins such as seafood, skinless poultry, lean beef, and soy products.
上面说，如果你在实行南海滩减肥法，你要专注于吃瘦肉蛋白，比如海鲜、去皮家禽、瘦牛肉和大豆制品。

1100
00:45:20.110 --> 00:45:27.570
You can also eat high-fiber vegetables, low-fat dairy foods with healthy, unsaturated fats, including avocados, nuts, and seeds.
你还可以吃高纤维蔬菜、低脂乳制品，以及含有健康不饱和脂肪的食物，包括牛油果、坚果和种子。

1101
00:45:27.990 --> 00:45:29.170
I'm going to start a diet.
我要开始减肥了。

1102
00:45:29.410 --> 00:45:30.430
What are you going to call it?
你打算给它取个什么名？

1103
00:45:30.570 --> 00:45:33.390
Just eat the good stuff and stop eating all the junk, everyone.
大家听着，就叫多吃好东西，别吃那些垃圾食品。

1104
00:45:33.650 --> 00:45:35.290
Is that too long of a diet title?
这个减肥名字是不是太长了？

1105
00:45:35.450 --> 00:45:38.830
Just, I mean, obviously, it's called just like f***ing common sense.
就是，我的意思是，很显然，这就叫他妈的常识。

1106
00:45:39.410 --> 00:45:40.390
Like, don't eat.
比如，别吃。

1107
00:45:40.390 --> 00:45:41.110
Don't be an idiot.
别当个白痴。

1108
00:45:41.230 --> 00:45:46.130
Yeah, just like eat stuff that grows out of the ground and lean protein the end.
对，就像吃那些从地里长出来的东西和瘦肉，就这样。

1109
00:45:46.370 --> 00:45:47.450
Every diet is the same.
所有减肥法都一样。

1110
00:45:47.630 --> 00:45:48.930
There's no difference in the diets.
这些减肥法根本没区别。

1111
00:45:49.330 --> 00:45:52.870
Like, how many different ways do we have to repackage the same information?
话说，我们还要把相同的信息重新包装多少次？

1112
00:45:53.090 --> 00:45:55.390
But then everyone's like, oh, I'm this diet.
但接着每个人都说，哦，我在搞这个减肥法。

1113
00:45:55.390 --> 00:45:56.110
I'm that diet.
我在搞那个减肥法。

1114
00:45:56.230 --> 00:45:57.450
And it's like, oh, what are you eating?
然后就好像是，哦，你在吃什么？

1115
00:45:57.630 --> 00:45:58.750
Oh, lean meat.
哦，瘦肉。

1116
00:45:58.750 --> 00:46:01.610
You're avoiding carbs and you're eating some fresh leafy vegetables.
