而且她很聪明，对科技产品也很在行。

1279
00:52:07.670 --> 00:52:11.650
You know, Angela, you played Andy's voicemail for us earlier.
安吉拉，你刚才给我们放了安迪的语音信箱。

1280
00:52:11.890 --> 00:52:12.090
Yeah.
对。

1281
00:52:12.090 --> 00:52:14.870
And we got some fan questions about it.
我们为此收到了一些粉丝的提问。

1282
00:52:15.050 --> 00:52:18.130
People thought maybe he was singing a jingle.
大家觉得他可能是在唱某个广告歌。

1283
00:52:18.370 --> 00:52:20.770
They wanted to know, like, what song is he really singing?
他们想知道，他唱的到底是什么歌？

1284
00:52:21.190 --> 00:52:23.010
I asked Steve Burgess about it.
我问过史蒂夫·伯吉斯了。

1285
00:52:23.090 --> 00:52:24.470
And he said Ed just made it up.
他说那是艾德自己瞎编的。

1286
00:52:24.550 --> 00:52:26.070
We didn't pay any rights for that melody.
我们可没为那个旋律买什么版权。

1287
00:52:26.210 --> 00:52:27.770
That's just an Ed Helms special.
那纯粹是艾德·赫尔姆斯的拿手好戏。

1288
00:52:27.770 --> 00:52:32.930
I 100% knew Ed made that up because he would make up little songs around the set.
我百分之百确信那是艾德瞎编的，因为他在片场就经常随口编一些小曲子。

1289
00:52:33.590 --> 00:52:37.150
And sometimes we would do all these little bits together, comedy bits.
有时候我们俩会一起整这些小包袱，喜剧小段子。

1290
00:52:37.430 --> 00:52:39.850
One day we were, like, walking into set at the same time.
有一天我们俩差不多同时走进片场。

1291
00:52:40.110 --> 00:52:42.310
And it was like, I don't know what we were doing.
当时就，我也不知道我们在干嘛。

1292
00:52:42.370 --> 00:52:45.310
But I said something like, oh, I forgot my Uggs.
但我随口说了句，哦，我忘穿雪地靴了。

1293
00:52:45.330 --> 00:52:47.370
And he's like, you forgot your Uggs.
他就说，你忘穿雪地靴了。

1294
00:52:47.430 --> 00:52:48.690
Gotta go get them.
得回去拿。

1295
00:52:48.850 --> 00:52:49.790
Or whatever it was.
诸如此类的吧。

1296
00:52:49.890 --> 00:52:51.110
It was something really silly.
就是些非常无厘头的事情。

1297
00:52:51.290 --> 00:52:51.690
Totally.
确实。

1298
00:52:51.690 --> 00:52:54.350
He could just make up a song at the drop of a hat.
他随时随地都能即兴编首歌。

1299
00:52:54.670 --> 00:52:56.610
Well, Andy's phone is going to keep ringing.
好了，安迪的电话要一直响个不停了。

1300
00:52:56.870 --> 00:52:58.170
He continues to ignore it.
他继续选择不接。

1301
00:52:58.410 --> 00:52:59.510
But Glenn answers it.
但格伦接了电话。

1302
00:52:59.610 --> 00:53:04.030
And this is where you see some of the way they wrote him to be just so obnoxious.
这就是你能看出他们把这个角色写得有多讨人厌的地方。

1303
00:53:04.430 --> 00:53:05.790
He answered the phone.
他接了电话。

1304
00:53:06.550 --> 00:53:07.030
Proctology.
肛肠科。

1305
00:53:08.390 --> 00:53:09.070
That's right.
没错。

1306
00:53:09.910 --> 00:53:10.930
And it's Jim.
然后是吉姆。

1307
00:53:11.050 --> 00:53:13.050
And he's like, Andy, where are you?
他说，安迪，你在哪儿？

1308
00:53:13.230 --> 00:53:18.070
And this is when Jim learns that Andy's not coming back, at least not without Aaron.
这时候吉姆得知安迪不会回来了，至少没有亚伦陪着是不会回来的。

1309
00:53:18.270 --> 00:53:19.070
He's in Florida.
他在佛罗里达。

1310
00:53:19.610 --> 00:53:23.010
So Jim is going to have to try to unify the group against Nellie.
所以吉姆必须设法团结大家对抗内莉。

1311
00:53:23.130 --> 00:53:28.910
He says we cannot participate in these performance reviews because then we are essentially accepting
他说我们绝不能参加这些绩效评估，因为那样我们基本上就等于接受了

1312
00:53:28.910 --> 00:53:29.830
her as our manager.
她担任我们的经理。

1313
00:53:30.450 --> 00:53:32.090
Dwight says he doesn't trust Nellie.
德怀特说他不信任内莉。

1314
00:53:32.250 --> 00:53:34.550
I mean, he wouldn't even trust her to run a celery farm.
我是说，他甚至不会信任她去经营一家芹菜农场。

1315
00:53:35.230 --> 00:53:35.670
Yes.
是的。

1316
00:53:35.950 --> 00:53:39.430
He has a talking head where he says those who can't farm, farm celery.
他有一段单独采访，说不会种地的人才去种芹菜。

1317
00:53:39.770 --> 00:53:41.830
Is this a dig on the celery community?
这是在嘲讽芹菜界吗？

1318
00:53:42.370 --> 00:53:43.890
Well, I had to know more.
嗯，我不得不深入了解一下。

1319
00:53:44.170 --> 00:53:49.830
I guess what he's referring to is that according to the internet, did you see what I did there,
我想他指的是，根据网上的说法，你发现我刚才的梗了吗，

1320
00:53:49.930 --> 00:53:50.150
Angela?
安吉拉？

1321
00:53:50.330 --> 00:53:52.670
I credited the whole internet just like how you do.
我把整个互联网都当成了信源，就像你平时做的那样。

1322
00:53:52.690 --> 00:53:53.050
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1323
00:53:53.190 --> 00:53:54.730
Because I forgot to write down my source.
因为我忘了写下我的出处。

1324
00:53:55.070 --> 00:53:59.210
I know the source sometimes, but sometimes there's multiple sources that say similar
我有时知道出处，但有时候有多个信源都说了类似的

1325
00:53:59.210 --> 00:53:59.610
things.
话。

1326
00:53:59.610 --> 00:54:01.490
So I just say according to the internet.
所以我干脆就说根据网上的说法。

1327
00:54:01.670 --> 00:54:02.090
All right.
好吧。

1328
00:54:02.090 --> 00:54:07.710
Well, according to the internet, as a lady who Googles, it turns out it's really quite
那么，根据网上的说法，作为一个爱用谷歌搜寻的女士，结果发现种芹菜其实相当

1329
00:54:07.710 --> 00:54:08.850
easy to grow celery.
容易。

1330
00:54:09.150 --> 00:54:10.850
It has very specific needs.
它有着非常特殊的需求。

1331
00:54:10.850 --> 00:54:12.070
You plant it in the spring.
你在春天把它种下。

1332
00:54:12.690 --> 00:54:17.970
You just have to give it a lot of water, have a good rich soil, and then in the fall, you
你只需要给它充足的水，准备肥沃的土壤，然后在秋天，

1333
00:54:17.970 --> 00:54:19.130
get a bunch of celery.
你就能收获一把芹菜。

1334
00:54:19.450 --> 00:54:22.710
I don't ever need to eat celery again for the rest of my life.
我这辈子再也不想吃芹菜了。

1335
00:54:23.090 --> 00:54:24.690
Josh puts it in soups.
乔希把它放进汤里。

1336
00:54:24.830 --> 00:54:25.910
I'm just like, great.
我只想说，太棒了。

1337
00:54:25.910 --> 00:54:28.210
Now I have a crunchy thing with no taste.
现在我得到了一个毫无味道的脆生生的东西。

1338
00:54:28.650 --> 00:54:29.570
I mean, come on.
我是说，拜托。

1339
00:54:29.570 --> 00:54:30.310
No taste?
没有味道？

1340
00:54:30.490 --> 00:54:31.590
Celery has a taste.
芹菜是有味道的。

1341
00:54:31.590 --> 00:54:32.470
What's the taste?
什么味道？

1342
00:54:32.790 --> 00:54:33.210
Celery.
芹菜味。

1343
00:54:33.970 --> 00:54:35.210
It tastes like celery.
它尝起来就是芹菜味。

1344
00:54:35.570 --> 00:54:38.330
It can't taste like something else or then it would be another thing.
它总不能尝起来像别的东西吧，否则它就是别的东西了。

1345
00:54:38.450 --> 00:54:39.530
It just tastes like celery.
它尝起来就是芹菜味。

1346
00:54:39.870 --> 00:54:40.390
It tastes like nothing.
它尝起来什么味道也没有。

1347
00:54:41.210 --> 00:54:41.570
Okay.
好吧。

1348
00:54:41.810 --> 00:54:42.390
If you get enough celery.
如果你吃够了芹菜的话。

1349
00:54:42.390 --> 00:54:44.530
Are you sure you're not thinking of like a water chestnut?
你确定你不是在想马蹄之类的东西吗？

1350
00:54:44.730 --> 00:54:46.110
Because those things taste like nothing.
因为那东西才真的是一点味道也没有。

1351
00:54:46.390 --> 00:54:46.910
Forget those.
忘掉那些吧。

1352
00:54:47.050 --> 00:54:47.770
I hate those too.
我也讨厌那些。

1353
00:54:48.690 --> 00:54:53.310
Celery, you know, if you crush up enough of it, you can have celery juice, but you just
西芹，你知道的，如果你把它榨得粉碎，就能喝到西芹汁，但你只是

1354
00:54:53.310 --> 00:54:56.010
chop a celery in half and take a bite of it, I get nothing.
把西芹切成两半咬上一口，我什么也尝不出来。

1355
00:54:56.010 --> 00:55:02.590
Do you remember the celery juice craze that hit California in like 2019?
你还记得大约 2019 年席卷加州的西芹汁热潮吗？

1356
00:55:03.030 --> 00:55:05.490
Everybody had celery juice.
每个人都在喝西芹汁。

1357
00:55:05.650 --> 00:55:07.150
They were walking around with it.
他们手里拿着它到处走。

1358
00:55:07.250 --> 00:55:08.050
I did it.
我当时也喝过。

1359
00:55:08.110 --> 00:55:09.170
And their big sippy cup things.
还有他们那种大大的吸管杯。

1360
00:55:09.170 --> 00:55:09.810
I did it.
我当时也喝过。

1361
00:55:10.030 --> 00:55:10.970
I did it.
我当时也喝过。

1362
00:55:11.070 --> 00:55:16.350
I was on splitting up together and me and Oliver Hudson, we did the celery juice craze.
我在拍《单身crossover》时，我和奥利弗·哈德森一起赶上了西芹汁热潮。

1363
00:55:16.350 --> 00:55:18.350
I don't know why we would do this.
我不知道我们为什么要这么做。

1364
00:55:18.510 --> 00:55:20.450
Is this part of your don't be an idiot diet?
这算是你的“别当个傻子”减肥法的一部分吗？

1365
00:55:20.610 --> 00:55:21.450
It could be.
也许吧。

1366
00:55:21.590 --> 00:55:22.510
It could be.
也许吧。

1367
00:55:23.030 --> 00:55:25.810
But there was this doctor, I guess.
但当时好像有个医生。

1368
00:55:26.070 --> 00:55:27.090
So there was...
所以当时……

1369
00:55:27.090 --> 00:55:27.790
There's always a doctor.
总会有个医生。

1370
00:55:27.930 --> 00:55:28.210
I know.
我知道。

1371
00:55:28.230 --> 00:55:29.010
There's always a doctor.
总会有个医生。

1372
00:55:29.390 --> 00:55:29.440
A doctor or something.
一个医生什么的。

1373
00:55:29.570 --> 00:55:30.550
I'm putting doctor in quotes.
我给“医生”打个引号。

1374
00:55:30.710 --> 00:55:31.210
I don't know.
我不知道。

1375
00:55:31.390 --> 00:55:33.770
Sorry, doctor who came up with celery juice.
抱歉，发明西芹汁的那个医生。

1376
00:55:33.870 --> 00:55:34.570
Maybe you're a real doctor.
也许你是个真正的医生。

1377
00:55:34.670 --> 00:55:35.070
I don't know.
我不知道。

1378
00:55:35.410 --> 00:55:40.850
But the idea was that you juice fresh celery first thing in the morning.
但这个说法的核心是，一大早就要把新鲜西芹榨汁。

1379
00:55:40.870 --> 00:55:42.890
You have to drink it on an empty stomach.
你必须空腹喝下它。

1380
00:55:43.330 --> 00:55:45.550
It sounds like it's going to just give you the runs.
听起来这只会让你拉肚子。

1381
00:55:47.070 --> 00:55:48.770
Well, it was interesting.
嗯，这挺有意思的。

1382
00:55:49.090 --> 00:55:52.750
It was supposed to be this miracle cure, like Kim Kardashian talked about it.
它本被吹捧为一种神奇的疗法，比如金·卡戴珊谈论过它。

1383
00:55:52.870 --> 00:55:54.530
Gwyneth Paltrow put it on Goop.
格温妮丝·帕特罗把它发在了 Goop 上。

1384
00:55:55.150 --> 00:55:56.570
And I don't know.
而且我不知道。

1385
00:55:56.750 --> 00:55:59.090
You know this happens on like TV and movie sets.
你知道这在电视和电影片场经常发生。

1386
00:55:59.450 --> 00:56:02.770
You get bored and then you do some fad.
你感到无聊，然后就会跟风赶时髦。

1387
00:56:02.870 --> 00:56:03.170
Yes.
是的。

1388
00:56:03.290 --> 00:56:05.350
I once did a show with Elijah Wood.
我曾经和伊利亚·伍德合作过一部剧。

1389
00:56:05.690 --> 00:56:11.910
I had a guest star on Wilfred and Randall Einhorn directed Little Office Reunion.
我在《路人甲》里客串过，兰德尔·艾因霍恩导演了《办公室小聚》。

1390
00:56:11.930 --> 00:56:15.990
And their whole thing on their set, and I learned it the first day,
他们在片场的全部乐趣——我第一天就知道了——

1391
00:56:15.990 --> 00:56:18.970
is everyone did crossword puzzles.
就是每个人都在玩填字游戏。

1392
00:56:19.850 --> 00:56:22.710
They would get the same crossword puzzle from the New York Times.
他们会从《纽约时报》打印出同一份填字游戏。

1393
00:56:22.850 --> 00:56:25.830
They'd print it out and everyone all day long would be doing the crossword.
他们把它打印出来，一整天所有人都在做填字。

1394
00:56:25.970 --> 00:56:27.450
And each day it gets harder.
而且一天比一天难。

1395
00:56:27.690 --> 00:56:31.750
We used to do the words with friends on our set when that came out.
那款游戏刚出来时，我们在片场经常玩“好友拼词”。

1396
00:56:31.750 --> 00:56:33.670
Well, you guys did celery juice.
好吧，你们喝的是西芹汁。

1397
00:56:33.670 --> 00:56:35.010
We did weird drinks.
我们喝的是奇怪的饮料。

1398
00:56:35.290 --> 00:56:35.590
Okay.
好吧。

1399
00:56:35.850 --> 00:56:38.310
Oliver and I did this weird tea for a while.
我和奥利弗有一阵子喝过一种奇怪的茶。

1400
00:56:38.310 --> 00:56:41.510
Now we started drinking celery juice in the mornings.
现在我们开始在早晨喝西芹汁了。

1401
00:56:42.030 --> 00:56:46.030
This whole craze, it created a shortage of celery.
这场全民狂热，造成了西芹短缺。

1402
00:56:46.470 --> 00:56:47.310
In California?
在加州吗？

1403
00:56:47.310 --> 00:56:48.070
In California.
在加州。

1404
00:56:48.070 --> 00:56:48.670
Yes.
是的。

1405
00:56:48.890 --> 00:56:50.950
I went and looked up an article on it.
我去查了一篇相关报道。

1406
00:56:51.370 --> 00:56:55.270
The LA Times said the sales increased by 350%.
《洛杉矶时报》说销量增长了350%。

1407
00:56:56.750 --> 00:56:59.470
Prices skyrocketed to as much as $5 a bunch.
价格暴涨，一束甚至高达5美元。

1408
00:56:59.750 --> 00:57:02.350
And there were pictures of like produce departments.
还有一些照片，比如农产品专区。

1409
00:57:02.410 --> 00:57:04.550
And then the celery part was empty.
然后西芹那部分全空了。

1410
00:57:05.490 --> 00:57:08.590
Because everybody started, you had to juice it fresh in the morning.
因为大家都开始……你得在早上榨新鲜的汁。

1411
00:57:08.650 --> 00:57:09.330
This was the other thing.
这就是另一回事了。

1412
00:57:09.430 --> 00:57:11.210
I was already going to work at 6 a.m.
我本来就要早上6点去上班。

1413
00:57:11.210 --> 00:57:15.330
But I was getting up even earlier to juice my celery.
但我起得更早，为了榨西芹汁。

1414
00:57:15.770 --> 00:57:17.390
And then you would drink it.
然后你把它喝下去。

1415
00:57:17.950 --> 00:57:18.970
Nothing happened.
什么都没发生。

1416
00:57:19.310 --> 00:57:21.610
You just, I mean, something happened.
你只是……我的意思是，确实发生了点什么。

1417
00:57:21.870 --> 00:57:24.470
But pretty much nothing happened.
但基本上什么都没发生。

1418
00:57:25.050 --> 00:57:27.910
Nothing in my life changed for this effort.
我的生活没有因为这份努力而发生任何改变。

1419
00:57:28.770 --> 00:57:30.190
I'm putting it in my book.
我要把它写进我的书里。

1420
00:57:30.330 --> 00:57:33.350
This is my theory on why I don't ever need to eat celery again.
这就是为什么我再也不需要吃西芹的理论。

1421
00:57:33.590 --> 00:57:37.410
I'm just saying, I guess, don't do silly things.
我只是想说，我猜，别做傻事。

1422
00:57:37.750 --> 00:57:38.890
Don't do fads.
别赶潮流。

1423
00:57:39.090 --> 00:57:41.090
You know what is good and you know what is bad.
你知道什么好，什么不好。

1424
00:57:41.210 --> 00:57:41.910
The end.
完结。

1425
00:57:42.230 --> 00:57:46.250
You sounded like a poem for like an elementary child.
你刚才听起来就像小学生读的诗。

1426
00:57:47.150 --> 00:57:48.290
It's that easy.
就是这么简单。

1427
00:57:48.510 --> 00:57:49.550
It's that easy.
就是这么简单。

1428
00:57:50.450 --> 00:57:52.730
Nellie is going to emerge from her new office.
内莉将从她的新办公室走出来。

1429
00:57:53.070 --> 00:57:55.450
It's time for her performance reviews to start.
她的绩效考核要开始了。

1430
00:57:55.890 --> 00:57:59.310
First up is the woman with the beautiful fingernails and tiny feet.
首先登场的是那个有着漂亮指甲和小脚的女人。

1431
00:57:59.910 --> 00:58:02.370
Angela starts to march towards the door.
安吉拉开始朝门走去。

1432
00:58:02.870 --> 00:58:03.870
It's Phyllis.
是菲利斯。

1433
00:58:03.990 --> 00:58:04.710
It's not Angela.
不是安吉拉。

1434
00:58:04.910 --> 00:58:05.510
It's Phyllis.
是菲利斯。

1435
00:58:05.690 --> 00:58:05.910
It's Phyllis.
是菲利斯。

1436
00:58:06.010 --> 00:58:07.190
And Phyllis says, you know what?
然后菲利斯说，你知道吗？

1437
00:58:07.190 --> 00:58:10.850
I don't feel comfortable being reviewed by someone that doesn't even know me.
我觉得被一个根本不了解我的人考核很不舒服。

1438
00:58:11.210 --> 00:58:12.470
Nellie says, that's fine.
内莉说，没关系。

1439
00:58:12.650 --> 00:58:13.390
That's fine.
没关系。

1440
00:58:13.530 --> 00:58:14.730
I'll show you how it's done.
我来给你示范一下怎么做。

1441
00:58:15.310 --> 00:58:15.710
Dwight.
德怀特。

1442
00:58:16.110 --> 00:58:18.130
Dwight says he also does not feel comfortable.
德怀特说他同样感到不舒服。

1443
00:58:18.450 --> 00:58:20.730
He lost all respect for her in Florida.
他在佛罗里达对她彻底失去了敬意。

1444
00:58:21.110 --> 00:58:23.090
So she just offers him a raise.
所以她直接给他提了薪。

1445
00:58:23.370 --> 00:58:23.710
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1446
00:58:23.710 --> 00:58:25.130
He deserves it.
这是他应得的。

1447
00:58:25.950 --> 00:58:29.030
Dwight obviously is going to agree that he deserves a raise.
德怀特显然会同意自己配得上加薪。

1448
00:58:29.210 --> 00:58:31.050
And Jim's like, the raise isn't real, Dwight.
吉姆则说，这加薪不是真的，德怀特。

1449
00:58:31.510 --> 00:58:34.790
And Dwight says money isn't real since they got off the gold standard.
德怀特说自从废除金银本位制后，钱就不是真的了。

1450
00:58:35.130 --> 00:58:39.410
And then he's going to start negotiating with Nellie about his raise.
然后他就要开始和内莉谈判他的加薪了。

1451
00:58:39.810 --> 00:58:41.690
He demands 5%.
他要求百分之五。

1452
00:58:41.690 --> 00:58:42.570
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1453
00:58:42.730 --> 00:58:44.730
She says, not good enough.
她说，还不够。

1454
00:58:45.050 --> 00:58:45.610
7%.
百分之七。

1455
00:58:45.610 --> 00:58:48.870
And then he says, no, 6%.
然后他说，不，百分之六。

1456
00:58:48.870 --> 00:58:49.990
I know my worth.
我知道我的价值。

1457
00:58:52.990 --> 00:58:54.210
Oh, I loved that.
哦，我太喜欢这个了。

1458
00:58:54.570 --> 00:58:56.970
Well, Phyllis now sees where this is going.
菲利斯现在看出事情的发展方向了。

1459
00:58:56.970 --> 00:58:59.050
So she's like, yeah, I'll get a review.
所以她的态度是，好吧，我要争取绩效评估。

1460
00:58:59.290 --> 00:58:59.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1461
00:59:00.110 --> 00:59:03.710
Nellie tells Phyllis that she's impressed with how she conquered her fear.
奈莉告诉菲利斯，她对菲利斯克服恐惧的表现印象深刻。

1462
00:59:04.090 --> 00:59:06.130
She even likes how she sits.
她甚至很喜欢她的坐姿。

1463
00:59:06.510 --> 00:59:07.370
So guess what?
所以你猜怎么着？

1464
00:59:07.430 --> 00:59:08.090
You get a raise.
你加薪了。

1465
00:59:09.250 --> 00:59:11.150
I guess that was a good first impression.
我猜那是给人的第一印象很好。

1466
00:59:11.470 --> 00:59:11.530
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1467
00:59:12.150 --> 00:59:14.990
Jim is going to go into the conference room and speak to Robert.
吉姆要走进会议室跟罗伯特谈谈。

1468
00:59:15.330 --> 00:59:19.230
He wants to make sure Robert knows that Nellie is just basically handing out raises.
他想确保罗伯特知道奈莉基本上是在随便发加薪。

1469
00:59:19.610 --> 00:59:23.570
And Robert's like, oh, I guess you want one so you can take the kids to Disney Town.
而罗伯特的反应是，哦，我猜你也想要加薪，好带孩子去迪士尼小镇吧。

1470
00:59:24.190 --> 00:59:24.750
Yeah.
是的。

1471
00:59:25.010 --> 00:59:26.890
He wants to give Jim a metaphor.
他想给吉姆一个比喻。

1472
00:59:27.350 --> 00:59:31.210
And the choices are nature metaphor or sexual metaphor.
选项是自然比喻或性比喻。

1473
00:59:31.710 --> 00:59:35.730
The nature metaphor includes animals having sex.
自然比喻包括动物交配。

1474
00:59:35.930 --> 00:59:36.270
Yeah.
是的。

1475
00:59:36.550 --> 00:59:41.030
The sex metaphor is that all life is sex and all sex is competition.
性比喻则是所有的生命都是性，而所有的性都是竞争。

1476
00:59:41.030 --> 00:59:42.330
There are no rules.
没有规则。

1477
00:59:42.970 --> 00:59:46.370
And Charles Darwin ultimately decides who the manager is.
最终是查尔斯·达尔文来决定谁当经理。

1478
00:59:46.550 --> 00:59:47.690
I summed it up.
我概括了一下。

1479
00:59:48.070 --> 00:59:51.850
That's how, I guess, Robert feels.
我猜罗伯特就是这么觉得的。

1480
00:59:52.730 --> 00:59:54.590
Robert talks about sex a lot.
罗伯特经常谈论性。

1481
00:59:55.030 --> 00:59:55.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1482
00:59:56.370 --> 00:59:56.830
Yeah.
是的。

1483
00:59:57.370 --> 01:00:00.330
It's really the lens through which he looks at the world.
这确实是他看待世界的视角。

1484
01:00:00.510 --> 01:00:00.830
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1485
01:00:00.970 --> 01:00:02.490
Well, thank you for summing that up.
好吧，谢谢你做了这个总结。

1486
01:00:02.750 --> 01:00:03.070
Yeah.
是的。

1487
01:00:03.190 --> 01:00:03.910
Jim is speechless.
吉姆说不出话来。

1488
01:00:04.470 --> 01:00:06.950
And Nellie is giving Kelly now a raise.
而奈莉现在正在给凯莉加薪。

1489
01:00:07.450 --> 01:00:08.690
So many raises.
加薪好多啊。

1490
01:00:09.210 --> 01:00:11.970
And now Dwight, he's sort of taking this all in.
现在德怀特，他有点把这一切都看在眼里。

1491
01:00:12.030 --> 01:00:12.570
He's like, you know what?
他心想，你知道吗？

1492
01:00:12.630 --> 01:00:13.430
Nellie's right.
奈莉是对的。

1493
01:00:13.810 --> 01:00:14.310
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1494
01:00:14.690 --> 01:00:20.430
So he, inspired by her, marches over to Daryl's office and says, hey, this is my office now.
所以他受到她的启发，大步走到达尔文的办公室说，嘿，现在这是我的办公室了。

1495
01:00:20.730 --> 01:00:21.770
And Daryl's like, no.
而达尔文说，不行。

1496
01:00:21.950 --> 01:00:22.790
And Dwight's like, yeah.
而德怀特说，行。

1497
01:00:22.950 --> 01:00:25.910
And then Daryl literally drags him out by his hair.
然后达尔文真的拽着他的头发把他拖了出去。

1498
01:00:26.290 --> 01:00:27.210
Dwight's like, well thought.
德怀特说，考虑得很周全。

1499
01:00:27.350 --> 01:00:28.630
I accept the outcome.
我接受这个结果。

1500
01:00:29.090 --> 01:00:31.890
And during all of this, Creed has taken Dwight's desk.
而在这一切发生的过程中，克里德已经占了德怀特的办公桌。

1501
01:00:32.150 --> 01:00:35.210
So Dwight actually lost a desk in this scenario.
所以德怀特在这种情况下实际上丢了一张桌子。

1502
01:00:35.650 --> 01:00:38.070
You know what I would have liked is if they would have held on to that.
你知道我希望的是什么吗，是他们能保留那个设定。

1503
01:00:38.270 --> 01:00:42.630
And then for like the rest of the season, Dwight was in the corner and Creed was across from Pam.
然后接下来的大半个季里，德怀特都坐在角落里，克里德坐在帕姆对面。

1504
01:00:42.890 --> 01:00:44.230
Oh, that would be pretty great.
哦，那一定挺棒的。

1505
01:00:44.810 --> 01:00:48.010
And Dwight just keeps waiting for Creed to get up so he can claim his chair.
而且德怀特一直在等克里德起身，这样他就能占回自己的椅子。

1506
01:00:48.130 --> 01:00:48.370
Yes.
没错。

1507
01:00:48.370 --> 01:00:49.730
I wish it would have become a runner.
我真希望这能变成一个贯穿全剧的常驻笑料。

1508
01:00:50.390 --> 01:00:53.750
Back in Florida, Andy is fixing Irene's fountain.
回到佛罗里达，安迪正在修理艾琳的喷泉。

1509
01:00:54.030 --> 01:00:56.790
And I spotted some birds of paradise for you, Angela.
安吉拉，我为你物色了一些天堂鸟花。

1510
01:00:57.030 --> 01:00:58.090
I spotted them too.
我也看到了。

1511
01:00:58.310 --> 01:00:59.610
It's a dolphin fountain.
这是一个海豚喷泉。

1512
01:00:59.970 --> 01:01:02.690
Erin says she's heard they're really beautiful when they work.
艾琳说她听说喷泉修好时真的很美。

1513
01:01:03.130 --> 01:01:07.070
Andy's been kind of hanging around, maybe hoping that Erin's going to change her mind.
安迪一直在附近晃悠，也许是希望艾琳能回心转意。

1514
01:01:07.270 --> 01:01:08.630
He had the hot dog lunch.
他吃了热狗午餐。

1515
01:01:08.630 --> 01:01:10.010
He did the leg exercises.
他做了腿部运动。

1516
01:01:10.010 --> 01:01:11.390
He's fixing the fountain.
他在修喷泉。

1517
01:01:11.910 --> 01:01:14.370
But Erin's going to come and confront him.
但艾琳马上要来找他摊牌了。

1518
01:01:14.930 --> 01:01:17.650
I would like to just point out something.
我想指出一件事。

1519
01:01:17.650 --> 01:01:24.870
In my opinion, this scene where Erin says, look, I care about you, but, you know, you hurt me.
在我看来，这场戏里艾琳说，听着，我在乎你，但是，你知道的，你伤害了我。

1520
01:01:25.330 --> 01:01:27.790
And he said, well, you also hurt me.
而他说，好吧，你也伤害了我。

1521
01:01:27.850 --> 01:01:29.630
And she goes, no, but you hurt me more times.
她说，不对，但你伤害我的次数更多。

1522
01:01:29.630 --> 01:01:31.670
I had to watch you date other people.
我不得不看着你跟别人约会。

1523
01:01:31.670 --> 01:01:33.430
You had to reject me over and over.
你却一次又一次地拒绝我。

1524
01:01:33.890 --> 01:01:42.650
I thought this scene was maybe the first time in so many episodes where Erin just seemed like a real person.
我觉得这场戏可能是很多集以来，艾琳第一次显得像个真正的人。

1525
01:01:42.830 --> 01:01:44.510
A very grounded person.
一个非常接地气的人。

1526
01:01:44.510 --> 01:01:50.230
Yes, not a caricature who doesn't know what papaya is.
对，不再是个连木瓜是什么都不知道的夸张滑稽角色。

1527
01:01:50.490 --> 01:01:51.110
Do you know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

1528
01:01:51.190 --> 01:01:52.650
Yeah, I do.
是的，我明白。

1529
01:01:53.210 --> 01:01:55.990
And I really liked Ellie's performance in this scene.
我真的很喜欢埃莉在这场戏里的表演。

1530
01:01:56.090 --> 01:01:56.650
I did too.
我也是。

1531
01:01:56.930 --> 01:01:58.190
It was very real.
非常真实。

1532
01:01:58.430 --> 01:02:00.290
I had a lot of empathy for Erin.
我对艾琳产生了很强的共鸣。

1533
01:02:00.710 --> 01:02:05.470
This is when I'm like, okay, in this moment, I root for Erin a little, right?
这时候我就想，好吧，在这瞬间，我有点支持艾琳了，对吧？

1534
01:02:06.450 --> 01:02:12.710
Because all the other times she didn't sound like a real person and Jessica seemed real.
因为其他时候她听起来都不像个真人，而杰西卡倒显得很真实。

1535
01:02:13.270 --> 01:02:16.830
Well, they're going to hug and Andy's going to leave.
嗯，他们接下来会拥抱，然后安迪就要离开了。

1536
01:02:17.130 --> 01:02:23.490
But then Erin is going to be so easily influenced, Irene is going to say, you're making a terrible mistake.
但接着艾琳太容易受影响了，艾琳老太太会说，你犯了个大错。

1537
01:02:23.930 --> 01:02:25.390
That guy seemed great.
那小伙子看起来挺棒的。

1538
01:02:25.930 --> 01:02:28.250
Even though she was being a real bee to him.
尽管她之前对安迪真够刻薄的。

1539
01:02:28.550 --> 01:02:28.950
Yeah.
是啊。

1540
01:02:29.270 --> 01:02:31.370
She was just trying to protect Erin.
她当时只是想保护艾琳。

1541
01:02:31.590 --> 01:02:32.890
But now she's like, you should go.
但现在她却说，你应该去。

1542
01:02:33.050 --> 01:02:33.830
You should go.
你应该去。

1543
01:02:34.050 --> 01:02:38.710
And just to finish up this storyline, I guess, Andy's driving away.
为了给这条故事线收尾，我想，安迪正开车离开。

1544
01:02:38.950 --> 01:02:43.490
And Erin is going to come running out of the house screaming, I love you.
然后艾琳会从屋里冲出来尖叫着喊我爱你。

1545
01:02:43.590 --> 01:02:44.770
She runs up to a Prius.
她跑向一台普锐斯。

1546
01:02:44.890 --> 01:02:45.610
She's like, don't leave.
她喊道，别走。

1547
01:02:45.610 --> 01:02:46.590
I love you.
我爱你。

1548
01:02:47.390 --> 01:02:48.350
Wrong Prius.
找错普锐斯了。

1549
01:02:48.350 --> 01:02:52.750
But then she finds him and they have an embrace in the middle of this intersection.
但随后她找到了他，他们在十字路口中间紧紧拥抱。

1550
01:02:53.130 --> 01:02:55.610
And they're going to drive off in the sunset together.
然后他们将一起驶向夕阳。

1551
01:02:55.890 --> 01:02:58.230
Her without any of the things she brought to Florida.
她身上没有带任何她去佛罗里达时随身携带的东西。

1552
01:02:58.230 --> 01:03:03.030
I'm assuming she had a suitcase for her time working for Saber.
我猜她为在赛博公司工作期间准备了一个手提箱。

1553
01:03:03.250 --> 01:03:03.650
Clothing.
衣服。

1554
01:03:04.370 --> 01:03:04.930
Toothbrush.
牙刷。

1555
01:03:05.430 --> 01:03:07.390
There's no rush, right?
不着急，对吧？

1556
01:03:07.590 --> 01:03:10.930
They could have gone back to the house for that bag pretty easily.
他们本可以很轻松地回屋去拿那个包。

1557
01:03:11.210 --> 01:03:14.430
There was in this scene a lot of driving choreography.
这场戏里有很多车辆调度的编排。

1558
01:03:14.430 --> 01:03:15.950
I was very impressed.
我印象非常深刻。

1559
01:03:15.950 --> 01:03:17.730
We had to shut down the street.
我们不得不封锁整条街。

1560
01:03:18.350 --> 01:03:19.950
There was the wrong Prius.
结果出现了一辆错的普锐斯。

1561
01:03:20.070 --> 01:03:22.350
There's two cars that drive by honking.
有两辆车开过去按了喇叭。

1562
01:03:22.730 --> 01:03:24.290
I asked Steve Burgess about it.
我问过史蒂夫·伯吉斯这件事。

1563
01:03:24.630 --> 01:03:26.590
I mean, this is complicated stuff.
我的意思是，这可真复杂。

1564
01:03:26.850 --> 01:03:32.050
Like, for us, this felt like a giant car chase fast and the furious.
对我们来说，这就感觉像是一场巨大的速度与激情式的汽车追逐戏。

1565
01:03:32.390 --> 01:03:32.870
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

1566
01:03:33.210 --> 01:03:34.270
Safety meeting.
安全会议。

1567
01:03:34.630 --> 01:03:35.470
Oh, for sure.
哦，肯定的。

1568
01:03:35.610 --> 01:03:35.770
Yeah.
是啊。

1569
01:03:36.230 --> 01:03:39.710
Steve Burgess said we got the extra Prius from the transpo department.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说那辆额外的普锐斯是从交通运输部门调来的。

1570
01:03:39.890 --> 01:03:41.310
He's not sure who was driving it.
他不太确定当时是谁在开。

1571
01:03:41.430 --> 01:03:44.650
But one of the cars was driven by our stand-in, Stephen Sox.
但其中一辆车是由我们的替身演员斯蒂芬·索克斯开的。

1572
01:03:44.970 --> 01:03:46.030
He was one of the honkers.
他就是按喇叭的人之一。

1573
01:03:46.630 --> 01:03:47.010
Nice.
不错。

1574
01:03:47.170 --> 01:03:47.470
I know.
我知道。

1575
01:03:47.590 --> 01:03:48.110
Go, Stephen.
加油，斯蒂芬。

1576
01:03:48.350 --> 01:03:48.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1577
01:03:49.150 --> 01:03:52.690
Well, back at Dunder Mifflin, Nellie is now going to win over Pam.
好了，镜头回到邓德米夫林，内莉现在要开始争取帕姆的支持了。

1578
01:03:53.410 --> 01:03:58.670
She's going to tell Pam, basically, that she's fantastic and deserves a nap.
她基本上是要告诉帕姆，她棒极了，值得好好睡个午觉。

1579
01:03:59.190 --> 01:03:59.670
Yeah.
是啊。

1580
01:03:59.990 --> 01:04:01.710
And, you know, it made me think.
而且，你知道的，这让我想到了...

1581
01:04:02.230 --> 01:04:07.390
I mean, I know Nellie's kind of coming out of left field here this episode, but she's
我的意思是，我知道内莉这集里有点像凭空杀出，但她

1582
01:04:07.390 --> 01:04:10.030
really good at reading her employees.
真的很擅长揣摩她的员工。

1583
01:04:10.750 --> 01:04:14.650
She's really good at knowing what they each want and how to butter them up.
她非常擅长摸清每个人的需求以及如何投其所好。

1584
01:04:14.790 --> 01:04:15.910
Isn't that a good manager?
这难道不是个好经理吗？

1585
01:04:15.910 --> 01:04:17.990
You're so right, Angela.
你太对了，安吉拉。

1586
01:04:18.350 --> 01:04:22.890
I mean, I know she doesn't know the company or anything else she's talking about, but she
我是说，我知道她根本不懂公司的事，也不懂她在说的其他任何东西，但她

1587
01:04:22.890 --> 01:04:26.650
seems to know how to relate one-on-one with people.
似乎很懂得如何与人一对一地建立联系。

1588
01:04:26.650 --> 01:04:27.790
She knows people.
她很懂人性。

1589
01:04:28.050 --> 01:04:28.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1590
01:04:28.590 --> 01:04:29.810
And so did Michael.
迈克尔也是这样。

1591
01:04:30.450 --> 01:04:31.230
That's right.
没错。

1592
01:04:31.690 --> 01:04:36.890
Did you notice that when she gets the pillow and blanket out of the little credenza, did
你有没有注意到，当她从那个小矮柜里拿出枕头和毯子时，你

1593
01:04:36.890 --> 01:04:40.470
you think that was like a Cornell blanket and pillow?
